00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:30.120
Too much technology.
科技含量太高了。

704
00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:30.980
Too much technology.
科技含量太高了。

705
00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:34.340
Because she goes to the big family computer and it doesn't work.
因为她走到那台大家庭电脑前，结果它坏了。

706
00:26:34.560 --> 00:26:38.920
Then she has a secret compartment in the bookshelf that she slides the doors open.
然后她在书架里发现了一个暗格，她把门滑开。

707
00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:41.100
And there's another smaller computer.
里面还有一台更小的电脑。

708
00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:43.620
And they video call Luke Skywalker.
接着他们和卢克·天行者进行了视频通话。

709
00:26:44.060 --> 00:26:45.060
He answers.
他接听了。

710
00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:46.300
He's with R2-D2.
他和R2-D2在一起。

711
00:26:46.460 --> 00:26:48.360
And I think we need to hear their phone call.
我觉得我们需要听听他们的通话内容。

712
00:26:48.460 --> 00:26:48.800
All right.
好吧。

713
00:26:50.060 --> 00:26:50.540
Hello.
喂。

714
00:26:54.310 --> 00:26:54.910
Where's Chewbacca?
楚巴卡在哪？

715
00:27:00.400 --> 00:27:01.120
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
哇，哇，哇。

716
00:27:01.220 --> 00:27:01.600
Wait a minute.
等一下。

717
00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:02.300
One at a time.
一个一个来。

718
00:27:16.680 --> 00:27:17.520
Not now, R2.
现在不行，R2。

719
00:27:21.540 --> 00:27:22.260
Oh, wait a minute.
噢，等一下。

720
00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:23.160
I don't like the looks of this.
我感觉不太对劲。

721
00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:23.900
Let me get this fixed.
让我把它修好。

722
00:27:26.550 --> 00:27:27.470
Your phone call.
你们的通话。

723
00:27:27.870 --> 00:27:28.410
That's it.
就是这样。

724
00:27:28.410 --> 00:27:31.790
If you want to know what the first 10 minutes of this movie are like.
如果你想知道这部电影前十分钟是什么样的话。

725
00:27:32.430 --> 00:27:33.230
That's it.
就是这样。

726
00:27:35.430 --> 00:27:43.310
Well, Luke is going to assure her that Han and Chewbacca are on their way despite the lack of communication.
卢克会向她保证，尽管联系不上，汉和楚巴卡已经在路上了。

727
00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:46.710
Because, come on, he's never missed a life day before.
因为拜托，他以前从没错过生命日。

728
00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:48.550
And he's not going to miss it this time.
这次他也不会错过的。

729
00:27:48.710 --> 00:27:50.010
He tells her to smile.
他让她笑一笑。

730
00:27:50.650 --> 00:27:53.150
What did I soapbox about, lady?
我刚才在那儿高谈阔论什么来着，女士？

731
00:27:53.490 --> 00:27:53.790
I know.
我知道。

732
00:27:54.110 --> 00:27:55.950
There's another one coming up, too.
后面还有一个呢。

733
00:27:55.950 --> 00:27:56.350
Oh, there is.
噢，确实有。

734
00:27:56.350 --> 00:27:57.150
I'm going to point out.
我正要指出来。

735
00:27:57.150 --> 00:27:58.070
I pointed it out.
我已经指出来了。

736
00:27:58.290 --> 00:27:59.450
It's that kiss.
就是那个吻。

737
00:28:00.590 --> 00:28:01.550
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

738
00:28:01.570 --> 00:28:02.390
I know.
我知道。

739
00:28:02.690 --> 00:28:03.050
Okay.
好的。

740
00:28:03.410 --> 00:28:03.770
Yeah.
是啊。

741
00:28:03.810 --> 00:28:04.990
He tells her to smile.
他让她笑一笑。

742
00:28:05.490 --> 00:28:10.370
Well, now Mala is going to reach out to Sean Dan.
好了，现在马拉要联系肖恩·丹了。

743
00:28:10.370 --> 00:28:14.110
Yeah, but, again, she's on the computer for a long time.
是啊，不过话说回来，她在电脑前待了很久。

744
00:28:14.110 --> 00:28:16.010
She has to type a bunch of stuff.
她得输入一大堆东西。

745
00:28:16.290 --> 00:28:17.950
Finally, it flashes up on the screen.
最后，屏幕上闪出了信息。

746
00:28:17.950 --> 00:28:20.790
It says, Trading Post Wookiee Planet C.
上面写着：贸易站伍基星球C。

747
00:28:21.310 --> 00:28:21.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

748
00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:24.910
And Sean Dan is played by Art Carney.
肖恩·丹是由阿特·卡尼饰演的。

749
00:28:25.870 --> 00:28:28.690
Art Carney was an actor and a comedian.
阿特·卡尼是一位演员兼喜剧演员。

750
00:28:29.230 --> 00:28:31.430
He was one of the stars of The Honeymooners.
他是《蜜月期》的主演之一。

751
00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:34.310
He played Ed Norton opposite Jackie Gleason.
他曾在《艾德·诺顿》中与杰基·格里森演对手戏。

752
00:28:34.810 --> 00:28:39.750
He was nominated for seven Emmy Awards, and he won six.
他曾七次获得艾美奖提名，并六次获奖。

753
00:28:40.150 --> 00:28:45.670
He also won an Academy Award and a Golden Globe in 1974.
1974年，他还获得了奥斯卡金像奖和金球奖。

754
00:28:45.970 --> 00:28:51.990
So right before this, he won an Academy Award and a Golden Globe for this movie, Harry and Tonto.
就在这之前，他凭借《哈里和托托》这部电影赢得了奥斯卡和金球奖。

755
00:28:52.270 --> 00:28:56.030
It's about an elderly man who goes on a road trip with his pet cat.
电影讲述了一位老人带着他的宠物猫去公路旅行的故事。

756
00:28:56.030 --> 00:28:58.570
I want you to hear the people he beat.
我想让你们听听他击败了哪些对手。

757
00:29:00.150 --> 00:29:04.890
Albert Finney, Dustin Hoffman, Jack Nicholson, and Al Pacino.
阿尔伯特·芬尼、达斯汀·霍夫曼、杰克·尼科尔森和阿尔·帕西诺。

758
00:29:05.110 --> 00:29:05.610
Wow.
哇。

759
00:29:05.970 --> 00:29:12.770
I just want everyone to understand the gravity of the actor that we got to play this role of Sean Dan.
我只是想让大家明白，我们请来饰演肖恩·丹这个角色的演员有多么重量级。

760
00:29:13.110 --> 00:29:13.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

761
00:29:13.770 --> 00:29:19.410
And his first line of dialogue, get ready for the beautiful writing here.
他的第一句台词，准备好欣赏这段优美的剧本吧。

762
00:29:19.830 --> 00:29:23.970
He says, oh, Imperial officer, I guess you'll want to see my identification.
他说：哦，帝国军官，我想你一定想看我的身份证件。

763
00:29:24.690 --> 00:29:25.410
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

764
00:29:26.150 --> 00:29:33.830
And then in a very deep voice, this Imperial officer, whose helmet kind of looks like a bonnet, and he has a really big mustache.
然后，那个帝国军官用一种非常低沉的声音说道——他的头盔看起来像顶软帽，还留着大胡子。

765
00:29:33.830 --> 00:29:35.650
He says, no, I'm off duty.
他说：不，我下班了。

766
00:29:35.810 --> 00:29:37.170
I've come to look at your shop.
我是来逛逛你的店的。

767
00:29:37.290 --> 00:29:39.790
He's got this really deep voice.
他的声音真的特别低沉。

768
00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:40.210
Yeah.
是啊。

769
00:29:40.290 --> 00:29:41.410
It cracked me up.
把我逗乐了。

770
00:29:41.970 --> 00:29:42.290
Yeah.
是啊。

771
00:29:42.450 --> 00:29:48.130
And Mala is going to call him while this officer is there.
就在这个军官在场的时候，玛拉要给他打电话。

772
00:29:48.130 --> 00:29:50.330
So they're going to have to kind of talk in code now.
所以他们现在得用暗语交流了。

773
00:29:50.590 --> 00:29:50.670
Yeah.
是啊。

774
00:29:51.290 --> 00:29:53.010
Because, you know, why?
因为，你知道，为什么呢？

775
00:29:53.030 --> 00:29:54.470
Why are they talking in code?
他们为什么要用暗语交流？

776
00:29:54.570 --> 00:29:55.650
This I did not understand.
这一点我没看懂。

777
00:29:56.010 --> 00:29:57.330
Why are they here?
他们为什么会在这儿？

778
00:29:57.570 --> 00:30:00.630
Why are they on this Wookiee planet?
他们为什么会在这个伍基人的星球上？

779
00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:04.330
Why don't they want Chewbacca to come home for life day?
他们为什么不想让丘巴卡回家过生命日？

780
00:30:04.530 --> 00:30:05.490
Why are we sneaking?
我们为什么要偷偷摸摸的？

781
00:30:05.750 --> 00:30:06.450
I don't get it.
我不明白。

782
00:30:06.630 --> 00:30:08.530
Well, Chewbacca is part of the resistance.
嗯，丘巴卡是抵抗组织的一员。

783
00:30:08.950 --> 00:30:10.790
So maybe there's that.
所以可能跟这个有关。

784
00:30:10.790 --> 00:30:14.770
At the end of Star Wars, didn't we get rid of all this Imperial business?
在《星球大战》结尾，我们不是已经摆脱了这些帝国势力了吗？

785
00:30:15.130 --> 00:30:15.890
Didn't that happen?
难道不是吗？

786
00:30:15.990 --> 00:30:16.510
Did we blow up?
我们不是炸毁了……？

787
00:30:16.550 --> 00:30:18.130
They blew up a whole planet, right?
他们炸毁了整个星球，对吧？

788
00:30:18.450 --> 00:30:18.730
Yeah.
是啊。

789
00:30:18.750 --> 00:30:20.430
Am I remembering this correctly?
我没记错吧？

790
00:30:20.830 --> 00:30:21.710
No, you're remembering it correctly.
不，你没记错。

791
00:30:21.710 --> 00:30:22.390
No, no, you're right.
不，不，你是对的。

792
00:30:22.390 --> 00:30:23.590
It doesn't make sense.
这根本说不通。

793
00:30:23.730 --> 00:30:28.710
After Star Wars and the happy ending of blowing up this planet, now in this Christmas special,
在《星球大战》炸毁星球的大团圆结局之后，现在在这个圣诞特辑里，

794
00:30:28.870 --> 00:30:32.670
I'm learning that we're under the thumb of the Imperial forces again.
我发现我们又被帝国势力压制了。

795
00:30:32.930 --> 00:30:33.970
Well, they blew up the Death Star.
嗯，他们是炸毁了死星。

796
00:30:33.970 --> 00:30:35.930
But they didn't obliterate the entire-
但他们并没有彻底消灭整个……

797
00:30:35.930 --> 00:30:37.810
They didn't get rid of the Imperial army.
他们并没有除掉帝国军队。

798
00:30:38.030 --> 00:30:41.250
But they got rid of almost everyone in it.
但他们几乎除掉了里面所有人。

799
00:30:41.390 --> 00:30:44.670
They got rid of their floating death ray machine.
他们除掉了那台漂浮的死亡射线机器。

800
00:30:44.830 --> 00:30:49.450
They had reorganized so quickly and have everyone under control again.
他们重组得太快了，又把所有人都控制住了。

801
00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:52.670
What was even the point of blowing up the Death Star?
炸掉死星到底有什么意义？

802
00:30:52.830 --> 00:30:58.070
Four seconds later, were everyone scared of the officers again?
四秒钟后，大家又开始怕那些军官了吗？

803
00:30:58.170 --> 00:30:59.810
Who's in charge, by the way?
顺便问一下，谁负责指挥？

804
00:30:59.870 --> 00:31:00.490
Who's in charge?
到底谁说了算？

805
00:31:00.490 --> 00:31:05.190
And why do we need to see this Imperial officer in a gadget shop?
还有，我们为什么要看这个帝国军官逛小商品店？

806
00:31:05.190 --> 00:31:06.770
He doesn't really like anything.
他其实什么都不喜欢。

807
00:31:07.010 --> 00:31:13.830
My favorite moment, I think we need to hear it, when we learn that you can buy a pocket aquarium.
我最喜欢的一个片段，我觉得大家得听听，就是我们发现原来还能买到袖珍水族箱的时候。

808
00:31:14.870 --> 00:31:17.230
Listen to his reaction to this gadget.
听听他对这个小玩意的反应。

809
00:31:18.230 --> 00:31:19.150
Ah, here we are.
啊，在这儿呢。

810
00:31:19.430 --> 00:31:19.870
Here it is.
就是这个。

811
00:31:20.830 --> 00:31:22.450
A pocket-sized aquarium.
袖珍水族箱。

812
00:31:23.310 --> 00:31:24.050
Wonderful, isn't it?
很棒，对吧？

813
00:31:28.690 --> 00:31:30.150
And you can take it with you anywhere.
而且你可以随身携带。

814
00:31:31.110 --> 00:31:32.950
And the tank is a snap to clean.
鱼缸清理起来也特别方便。

815
00:31:33.090 --> 00:31:34.310
I hate fish.
我讨厌鱼。

816
00:31:34.310 --> 00:31:41.070
I'm telling you, I live for this guy.
我跟你说，我就是为了看这家伙才活着的。

817
00:31:41.410 --> 00:31:43.630
His voice, his reaction to everything.
他的声音，他对每件事的反应。

818
00:31:43.670 --> 00:31:45.050
This scene is bonkers.
这一幕简直疯了。

819
00:31:45.830 --> 00:31:53.390
Well, at the end of the scene, Sean Dan is going to convince the officer that he needs this special groomer.
好了，在这一幕结束时，肖恩·丹会说服军官他需要这个特殊的修剪器。

820
00:31:53.890 --> 00:31:58.370
And he's going to discuss the multiple uses of the groomer with the officer.
他会和军官讨论这个修剪器的多种用途。

821
00:31:58.530 --> 00:31:59.930
He's going to make a sale.
他会成功卖出去的。

822
00:32:00.250 --> 00:32:02.050
And I'd like us to hear it.
我想让我们听听这段。

823
00:32:02.050 --> 00:32:03.730
Just a groomer, you say?
你说这只是个修剪器？

824
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:11.720
Evidently, you haven't read the instructions, the warranty and the guarantee.
显然，你还没读过说明书、保修单和保证书。

825
00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:16.800
Besides shaving and hair trimming, it's guaranteed to lift stains off clothing, faces and hands.
除了剃须和修剪毛发，它还能保证去除衣服、脸部和手上的污渍。

826
00:32:17.180 --> 00:32:18.740
Cleans teeth, fingers and toenails.
能清洁牙齿、手指和脚趾甲。

827
00:32:19.120 --> 00:32:19.680
Washes eyes.
能清洗眼睛。

828
00:32:19.980 --> 00:32:20.560
Pierces ears.
能穿耳洞。

829
00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:23.000
Calculates, modulates and syncopates life rhythMs.
能计算、调节并同步生活节奏。

830
00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:28.860
And can repeat the entire Imperial Penal Code, all 17 volumes, in half the time of the old XP-2-1.
而且能背诵整部帝国刑法，全套17卷，速度是旧款XP-2-1的一半。

831
00:32:30.140 --> 00:32:32.120
Just the thing to keep you squeaky clean.
这正是让你保持一尘不染的神器。

832
00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:38.000
And you guys, if you see it, it's like a stick with a brush on the end.
伙计们，如果你们看到了，它就像一根顶端带着刷子的棍子。

833
00:32:39.840 --> 00:32:40.640
Capulate, modulate.
计算，调节。

834
00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:47.020
Well, after this, we are going to cut to Darth Vader.
好了，在这之后，我们要切到达斯·维达的镜头。

835
00:32:47.540 --> 00:32:47.980
Yeah.
是啊。

836
00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:49.240
How exciting.
多令人兴奋啊。

837
00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:50.420
Very exciting.
非常令人兴奋。

838
00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:59.560
Darth Vader tells his henchmen that he wants to find and identify the rebels, even if it means searching every home in the system.
达斯·维达告诉他的手下，他要找到并确认那些反叛军，哪怕这意味着要搜查星系里的每一户人家。

839
00:32:59.900 --> 00:33:00.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

840
00:33:00.640 --> 00:33:02.220
I have a fun fact for you.
我有个有趣的事实要告诉你。

841
00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:02.660
What?
什么？

842
00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:09.460
James Earl Jones is the voice of Darth Vader, but he was originally uncredited in the Star Wars movies.
詹姆斯·厄尔·琼斯是达斯·维达的配音，但他最初在《星球大战》电影中并没有署名。

843
00:33:09.460 --> 00:33:14.540
So this special marks the first time he was actually credited as the voice of Darth Vader.
所以这部特辑标志着他第一次真正以达斯·维达配音演员的身份出现在演职员表中。

844
00:33:14.820 --> 00:33:16.560
Oh, I have a tidbit for you.
哦，我也有个小道消息告诉你。

845
00:33:16.680 --> 00:33:17.100
What is it?
是什么？

846
00:33:17.700 --> 00:33:19.900
Apparently, George Lucas is not in the credits.
显然，乔治·卢卡斯不在演职员表里。

847
00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:21.100
He's not?
真的吗？

848
00:33:21.800 --> 00:33:22.840
That's what I read.
我是这么读到的。

849
00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:23.740
Hmm.
嗯。

850
00:33:24.120 --> 00:33:25.080
I didn't notice.
我没注意到。

851
00:33:25.340 --> 00:33:25.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

852
00:33:27.480 --> 00:33:34.120
We're going to go back to the Wookiee home because that's where most of the special is set.
我们要回到伍基人的家，因为特辑的大部分内容都发生在那里。

853
00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:34.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

854
00:33:34.840 --> 00:33:36.000
Mala is busy cooking.
玛拉正在忙着做饭。

855
00:33:36.460 --> 00:33:38.060
She's watching a cooking show.
她正在看烹饪节目。

856
00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:38.540
Yeah.
没错。

857
00:33:38.540 --> 00:33:47.240
She is watching Gormanda, who is played by Harvey Korman, sort of a take on Julia Child, I think.
她看的是戈曼达，由哈维·科曼饰演，我觉得这有点模仿朱莉娅·查尔德。

858
00:33:47.400 --> 00:33:49.980
This is one of his three characters he plays.
这是他饰演的三个角色之一。

859
00:33:50.340 --> 00:33:50.800
Yes.
是的。

860
00:33:51.040 --> 00:33:55.400
Harvey Korman rose to fame thanks to his role on The Carol Burnett Show.
哈维·科曼因在《卡罗尔·伯内特秀》中的角色而声名鹊起。

861
00:33:55.880 --> 00:34:01.660
During his 10-year run on the show, he received six Emmy nominations, and he won four.
在该节目播出的十年间，他获得了六次艾美奖提名，并赢得了四次。

862
00:34:01.660 --> 00:34:08.720
He also starred in the Mel Brooks films Blazing Saddles and High Anxiety and the Disney film Herbie Goes Bananas.
他还出演了梅尔·布鲁克斯的电影《灼热的马鞍》和《高压危机》，以及迪士尼电影《金龟车大闹南美洲》。

863
00:34:09.100 --> 00:34:13.260
And I was relieved when this bit came up.
当这一段出现时，我松了一口气。

864
00:34:13.400 --> 00:34:15.880
I did appreciate this comedy bit.
我确实很欣赏这段喜剧表演。

865
00:34:15.880 --> 00:34:17.680
Well, that's what he's there for.
嗯，他就是为此而来的。

866
00:34:17.900 --> 00:34:18.220
Yes.
是的。

867
00:34:18.460 --> 00:34:23.740
He is wearing a gray sort of pompadour wig with a pink dress and a cape.
他戴着一顶灰色的蓬巴杜假发，穿着粉红色的裙子，披着斗篷。

868
00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:27.120
His hands have these big gloves that come up.
他的手上戴着那种长到手臂的大手套。

869
00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:27.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

870
00:34:28.060 --> 00:34:29.980
There might be more hands coming.
可能还会有更多只手出现。

871
00:34:30.180 --> 00:34:30.920
There will be.
确实会有。

872
00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:36.740
Chef Gormanda is teaching you how to make Bantha Surprise.
戈曼达厨师正在教你如何制作班萨惊喜。

873
00:34:36.740 --> 00:34:43.660
This is a traditional dish served on Life Day, and Mala is following the instructions.
这是生命日的一道传统菜肴，玛拉正在按照说明操作。

874
00:34:43.860 --> 00:34:48.400
It seems like the way you make it is you just kind of whip things into a frenzy.
看起来制作方法就是把各种东西搅在一起，搅到疯狂。

875
00:34:49.200 --> 00:34:49.760
Yes.
是的。

876
00:34:50.080 --> 00:34:51.080
Here's an audio clip.
这是一段音频片段。

877
00:34:52.880 --> 00:34:55.820
Step one, we stir the mixture.
第一步，我们搅拌混合物。

878
00:34:56.460 --> 00:35:01.400
Stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir.
搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅。

879
00:35:01.420 --> 00:35:01.800
Very nice.
非常好。

880
00:35:06.740 --> 00:35:14.200
Stir, whip, whip, whip, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir,
搅，打，打，打，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，

881
00:35:14.200 --> 00:35:27.060
stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir, stir,
搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，搅，

882
00:35:27.060 --> 00:35:27.580
Whip, stir.
打，搅。

883
00:35:27.860 --> 00:35:29.140
Come on, faster, all together now.
来吧，快点，大家一起。

884
00:35:29.300 --> 00:35:30.180
Cooking can be fun.
烹饪也可以很有趣。

885
00:35:30.460 --> 00:35:33.080
Stir, whip, stir, whip, whip, whip, stir.
搅，打，搅，打，打，打，搅。

886
00:35:33.420 --> 00:35:36.100
Stir, whip, stir, whip, whip, whip, stir.
搅，打，搅，打，打，打，搅。

887
00:35:36.340 --> 00:35:36.520
Wah!
哇！

888
00:35:37.280 --> 00:35:38.060
There you go.
这就对了。

889
00:35:38.360 --> 00:35:38.620
Yeah.
没错。

890
00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:44.360
And during all the stirring and whipping, Gourmanda gets a third arm and then a fourth arm.
在所有的搅拌和抽打过程中，戈曼达长出了第三只手，然后是第四只手。

891
00:35:44.480 --> 00:35:46.500
Yeah, well, here's what happens.
是啊，事情是这样的。

892
00:35:46.860 --> 00:35:49.700
After that segment, Gourmanda's like, you also got to beat it.
在那段之后，戈曼达说，你还得把它打匀。

893
00:35:49.820 --> 00:35:51.540
So then another arm comes out to beat it.
于是又伸出另一只手来打。

894
00:35:51.640 --> 00:35:52.840
And then you've got to taste it.
然后你还得尝一尝。

895
00:35:52.940 --> 00:35:54.260
And another comes out to taste it.
于是又伸出一只手来尝。

896
00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:55.620
And then there's four arms going.
最后四只手同时在动。

897
00:35:55.620 --> 00:35:56.920
This is comedy gold.
这简直是喜剧经典。

898
00:35:57.620 --> 00:36:02.540
I mean, Harvey is trying to keep up that one of the arms is feeding him.
我是说，哈维试图跟上节奏，其中一只手还在喂他吃。

899
00:36:02.640 --> 00:36:03.360
The other one's whipping.
另一只在打。

900
00:36:03.540 --> 00:36:04.220
The other one's stirring.
还有一只在搅。

901
00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:05.000
One's beating.
有一个在跳动。

902
00:36:05.300 --> 00:36:07.200
His wig starts to fall apart.
他的假发开始散架了。

903
00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:09.500
I mean, hilarious.
我是说，太搞笑了。

904
00:36:10.320 --> 00:36:13.660
Angela, did you know what Banthas were?
安吉拉，你知道班萨是什么吗？

905
00:36:14.060 --> 00:36:17.660
They serve as mounts for Tuscan raiders.
它们是塔斯肯袭击者的坐骑。

906
00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:21.620
And the two share a close, almost mystical bond.
两者之间有着紧密的、近乎神秘的联系。

907
00:36:22.220 --> 00:36:23.840
But Wookiees eat them.
但伍基人会吃它们。

908
00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:25.680
Yeah, they have big horns.
对，它们有大角。

909
00:36:25.680 --> 00:36:26.780
They're like giant sheep.
它们就像巨大的绵羊。

910
00:36:26.780 --> 00:36:27.960
Oh, that's right.
哦，没错。

911
00:36:27.960 --> 00:36:28.860
That's what they are.
它们就是那样的。

912
00:36:28.940 --> 00:36:29.720
And they ride them.
而且他们会骑着它们。

913
00:36:29.940 --> 00:36:33.080
They look like a giant, like, sheep, woolly mammoth.
它们看起来就像巨大的，呃，绵羊，长毛猛犸象。

914
00:36:33.080 --> 00:36:34.060
I know what they are now.
我现在知道它们是什么了。

915
00:36:34.100 --> 00:36:34.480
Combo.
组合。

916
00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:35.860
I just didn't know the name.
我只是不知道名字而已。

917
00:36:35.980 --> 00:36:36.800
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

918
00:36:36.980 --> 00:36:37.300
What?
什么？

919
00:36:37.480 --> 00:36:39.640
Is this kind of like eating a horse then?
那这就像是吃马肉吗？

920
00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:46.540
I mean, it feels like it's eating a unicorn because the thing has a mystical bond with its rider.
我是说，感觉就像在吃独角兽，因为那东西和它的骑手有种神秘的联系。

921
00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:49.460
Or eating a dragon or eating a dragon or something.
或者吃龙，或者吃龙之类的东西。

922
00:36:49.820 --> 00:36:51.600
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

923
00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:53.260
But the Wookiees love it.
但伍基人很喜欢吃。

924
00:36:53.420 --> 00:37:02.620
I'll have you all know that if you would like, you can purchase the Star Wars Life Day Cookbook.
我要告诉大家，如果你们愿意，可以去买《星球大战生命日食谱》。

925
00:37:02.620 --> 00:37:05.040
I'm holding it in my hands right now.
我现在正拿在手里。

926
00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:10.800
It contains, quote, official holiday recipes from a galaxy far, far away.
里面包含了，引用一下，“来自遥远银河系的官方节日食谱”。

927
00:37:11.120 --> 00:37:15.220
And this was released after the holiday special.
这是在节日特辑之后发布的。

928
00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:25.640
And there is a recipe for Bantha surprise, which I thought maybe Josh could make for us.
里面有个“班萨惊喜”的食谱，我想也许乔什能为我们做。

929
00:37:25.640 --> 00:37:26.420
Yes.
是的。

930
00:37:26.780 --> 00:37:27.680
And he did.
他也确实做了。

931
00:37:28.860 --> 00:37:30.040
Jenna emailed Josh.
珍娜给乔什发了邮件。

932
00:37:30.200 --> 00:37:33.200
Josh was like, Ange, I just got a really weird email from Jenna.
乔什说，安吉，我刚收到珍娜发来的一封很奇怪的邮件。

933
00:37:33.440 --> 00:37:34.420
I was like, what do you mean?
我说，你什么意思？

934
00:37:34.660 --> 00:37:38.420
She was like, she wants me to make a type of stew for the podcaSt.
她说，她想让我为播客做一种炖菜。

935
00:37:38.920 --> 00:37:39.400
Yeah.
是的。

936
00:37:39.580 --> 00:37:44.400
If you look at the recipe, it is basically a recipe for beef stew.
如果你看那个食谱，它基本上就是炖牛肉的食谱。

937
00:37:44.600 --> 00:37:44.880
Yes.
是的。

938
00:37:45.020 --> 00:37:47.200
It's got carrots and onions, celery.
里面有胡萝卜、洋葱和芹菜。

939
00:37:48.180 --> 00:37:50.380
And so I'm excited to try it.
所以我很期待尝尝看。

940
00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:51.300
I brought it today.
我今天带来了。

941
00:37:51.300 --> 00:37:56.400
Well, the human version, the recipe calls for beef rather than Bantha.
嗯，人类版本，食谱里用的是牛肉而不是班萨肉。

942
00:37:56.720 --> 00:38:00.140
And Cassie, I know you're a vegetarian and you won't be able to partake.
凯西，我知道你是素食主义者，不能吃这个。

943
00:38:00.200 --> 00:38:07.120
So I did make us a special punch, according to the Life Day Cookbook that you can have.
所以我根据《生命日食谱》为我们特制了一种你可以喝的潘趣酒。

944
00:38:07.420 --> 00:38:10.520
It's called Joe Blasto Punch.
它叫乔·布拉斯托潘趣酒。

945
00:38:10.820 --> 00:38:11.200
Oh.
哦。

946
00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:13.300
Do you know who Joe Blasto is?
你知道乔·布拉斯托是谁吗？

947
00:38:13.580 --> 00:38:19.900
I guess Joe Blasto is a classic Husties Life Day jingle.
我猜乔·布拉斯托是一首经典的赫斯蒂生命日短曲。

948
00:38:20.480 --> 00:38:21.680
It's a song.
那是一首歌。

949
00:38:22.120 --> 00:38:24.720
Joe Blasto is a song, not a person.
乔·布拉斯托是一首歌，不是一个人。

950
00:38:24.940 --> 00:38:26.180
I guess it's a song.
我想它是一首歌。

951
00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:27.600
It's not in the special.
它不在特别节目里。

952
00:38:27.840 --> 00:38:29.340
The song is not in the special.
这首歌不在特别节目里。

953
00:38:29.720 --> 00:38:31.220
You sing it on Life Day?
你在生命日唱它吗？

954
00:38:31.540 --> 00:38:32.060
Yeah.
是的。

955
00:38:32.260 --> 00:38:35.200
And then here are the words in the cookbook.
然后这是食谱里的歌词。

956
00:38:35.400 --> 00:38:36.260
Oh, sing it.
哦，唱出来吧。

957
00:38:36.500 --> 00:38:36.920
Okay.
好吧。

958
00:38:37.720 --> 00:38:39.140
Make up your own tune.
你自己编个曲调。

959
00:38:39.240 --> 00:38:42.300
It's written in both Wookiee and English.
它既有伍基语版本，也有英语版本。

960
00:38:42.320 --> 00:38:47.000
Do you want me to do the Wookiee part with my mask and you do the English part?
你想让我戴着面具唱伍基语部分，你唱英语部分吗？

961
00:38:47.440 --> 00:38:47.920
Sure.
当然。

962
00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:48.340
Okay.
好。

963
00:38:48.340 --> 00:38:50.540
I don't know the melody.
我不知道旋律。

964
00:38:51.480 --> 00:39:03.840
Rumor has it that R3X, the DJ droid over at Oga's Cantina, has a collection of Joe Blasto remixes so extensive that it could play all life day without ever repeating.
有传言说，奥加酒馆的DJ机器人R3X收藏了海量的乔·布拉斯托混音曲，甚至可以整整一个生命日循环播放都不带重样的。

965
00:39:04.840 --> 00:39:06.680
So here's the Wookiee.
那这是伍基语部分。

966
00:39:06.740 --> 00:39:11.220
I love that you're standing over my shoulder as if this means anything to you.
我真喜欢你站在我肩后，好像这东西对你有什么意义似的。

967
00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:15.680
And I'll sing this part in a melody that I make up on the spot.
然后我会用我当场编的旋律唱这一段。

968
00:39:15.680 --> 00:39:17.720
And then I'll sing the Wookiee part.
接着我会唱伍基语部分。

969
00:39:17.920 --> 00:39:18.360
Yeah, sure.
行，没问题。

970
00:39:18.500 --> 00:39:19.200
Over my shoulder.
站在我肩后。

971
00:39:19.400 --> 00:39:19.540
Okay.
好的。

972
00:39:19.820 --> 00:39:20.440
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

973
00:39:20.640 --> 00:39:20.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

974
00:39:21.820 --> 00:39:25.340
Joe Blasto, Joe Blasto, Blasto.
乔·布拉斯托，乔·布拉斯托，布拉斯托。

975
00:39:26.040 --> 00:39:30.200
Muli-ra, o-ta-pan-wa-yat-a-ka.
穆里-拉，欧-塔-潘-瓦-雅-塔-卡。

976
00:39:31.620 --> 00:39:33.580
Bo, e-o-bi-chopa.
波，伊-欧-比-乔帕。

977
00:39:34.420 --> 00:39:36.500
Ji-ba-la-kai-ya-toop.
吉-巴-拉-凯-雅-图普。

978
00:39:36.520 --> 00:39:37.080
I can't.
我唱不下去。

979
00:39:37.160 --> 00:39:37.760
I can't.
我唱不下去。

980
00:39:37.860 --> 00:39:38.800
That's all I can do.
我只能做到这样了。

981
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:39.760
That's all I can do.
我只能做到这样了。

982
00:39:39.760 --> 00:39:40.940
No one wants to hear that.
没人想听那个。

983
00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:44.020
No one wants to hear us do that.
没人想听我们唱那个。

984
00:39:44.260 --> 00:39:45.240
I apologize.
我很抱歉。

985
00:39:46.640 --> 00:39:48.740
I don't even want to hear us do that.
连我自己都不想听我们唱那个。

986
00:39:48.820 --> 00:39:53.320
I, I, I, everyone.
我，我，我，各位。

987
00:39:57.270 --> 00:39:58.870
Well, that was special.
嗯，那真是太“特别”了。

988
00:39:59.170 --> 00:40:02.470
We've now just made our own show holiday special.
我们刚刚自制了一档节目特别篇。

989
00:40:03.050 --> 00:40:05.010
Everybody, we are going to take a break.
各位，我们要休息一下。

990
00:40:05.210 --> 00:40:06.750
We're going to get out the Bantha surprise.
我们要去端出班萨惊喜料理。

991
00:40:06.750 --> 00:40:12.010
I'm going to get out the Joe Blasto punch, and we'll be right back.
我要去拿乔·布拉斯托潘趣酒，我们马上回来。

992
00:40:25.540 --> 00:40:26.540
Okay, everyone.
好了，各位。

993
00:40:26.540 --> 00:40:27.480
We're back.
我们回来了。

994
00:40:27.680 --> 00:40:30.400
We've got our Bantha surprise.
我们拿到了班萨惊喜料理。

995
00:40:30.820 --> 00:40:31.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

996
00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:32.140
Our stew.
我们的炖菜。

997
00:40:32.620 --> 00:40:33.980
And we have our punch.
还有我们的潘趣酒。

998
00:40:34.100 --> 00:40:35.640
Ainsley is also a vegetarian.
安斯利也是素食主义者。

999
00:40:35.640 --> 00:40:40.180
So, Sam, Angela, let's try our Bantha surprise.
所以，萨姆，安吉拉，我们来尝尝班萨惊喜料理吧。

1000
00:40:40.580 --> 00:40:41.440
Here I go.
我来了。

1001
00:40:45.920 --> 00:40:47.260
I mean, it's stew.
我的意思是，这就是炖菜。

1002
00:40:47.420 --> 00:40:47.480
Right.
没错。

1003
00:40:47.780 --> 00:40:48.740
It's a beef stew.
这是牛肉炖菜。

1004
00:40:48.960 --> 00:40:49.380
This is great.
这太棒了。

1005
00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:49.960
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1006
00:40:50.440 --> 00:40:50.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1007
00:40:51.080 --> 00:40:52.000
Highly recommend.
强烈推荐。

1008
00:40:52.960 --> 00:40:56.060
If you base the movie off of this, this movie's great.
如果电影是根据这个来拍的，那电影肯定很棒。

1009
00:40:56.360 --> 00:40:57.220
Movie is terrific.
电影太赞了。

1010
00:40:57.480 --> 00:40:57.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1011
00:40:57.800 --> 00:40:59.940
We'll, we'll put the recipe in our stories.
我们会把食谱发到我们的快拍里。

1012
00:41:00.400 --> 00:41:02.100
And Josh, we'll show you how to make it.
还有乔什，我们会教你怎么做。

1013
00:41:02.880 --> 00:41:03.200
All right.
好的。

1014
00:41:03.420 --> 00:41:05.480
Now, let me try my punch.
现在，让我尝尝我的潘趣酒。

1015
00:41:05.700 --> 00:41:06.300
I think I-
我觉得我——

1016
00:41:06.300 --> 00:41:08.060
By the way, the punch, I should tell you what's in it.
顺便说一下，这酒，我得告诉你里面有什么。

1017
00:41:08.700 --> 00:41:09.080
Right?
对吧？

1018
00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:10.900
Let's see.
让我想想。

1019
00:41:10.900 --> 00:41:12.300
This punch is insane, by the way.
顺便说一句，这酒简直绝了。

1020
00:41:13.340 --> 00:41:14.420
Insane in a good way?
是好喝的那种绝吗？

1021
00:41:14.680 --> 00:41:15.920
I need a sip of water.
我需要喝口水。

1022
00:41:16.020 --> 00:41:18.880
I don't think I can go from beef stew to this.
我觉得我没法从牛肉炖菜直接过渡到这个。

1023
00:41:18.880 --> 00:41:22.860
It looks like, it looks like a rainbow ice cream in a cup.
它看起来，看起来就像杯子里的彩虹雪酪。

1024
00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:24.720
Well, here's what it is.
好吧，它是这样的。

1025
00:41:24.920 --> 00:41:28.320
It is cranberry juice, pineapple juice, 7-Up.
它是蔓越莓汁、菠萝汁和七喜。

1026
00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:34.300
And then you mix that together and you top it with a scoop of rainbow sherbet.
然后把它们混合在一起，上面再加一勺彩虹雪酪。

1027
00:41:34.500 --> 00:41:35.000
Woo-hoo.
呜呼。

1028
00:41:35.300 --> 00:41:35.800
Here we go.
开始了。

1029
00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:36.560
Okay.
好的。

1030
00:41:36.560 --> 00:41:39.420
Everybody, and Ainsley, Cassie, you've got some.
大家，还有安斯利、卡西，你们也来点。

1031
00:41:40.700 --> 00:41:41.020
Woo!
呜！

1032
00:41:41.380 --> 00:41:42.280
I told you.
我早跟你说了。

1033
00:41:43.040 --> 00:41:44.260
No, this isn't a game.
不，这可不是闹着玩的。

1034
00:41:44.540 --> 00:41:44.680
Woo!
呜！

1035
00:41:44.980 --> 00:41:45.820
Okay, here we go.
好了，开始吧。

1036
00:41:45.980 --> 00:41:48.040
It was more tart than I expected.
比我预想的要酸得多。

1037
00:41:48.440 --> 00:41:49.840
The combination of-
这种组合——

1038
00:41:49.840 --> 00:41:50.680
Oh, my Lord.
天哪。

1039
00:41:50.960 --> 00:41:53.400
Of, like, rich beef stew.
像这种浓郁的牛肉炖菜。

1040
00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:56.860
I can't believe you didn't take a sip of water between the two.
真不敢相信你在两者之间竟然没喝口水。

1041
00:41:57.320 --> 00:41:58.860
Chased with this punch?
喝完炖菜接着喝这酒？

1042
00:41:59.360 --> 00:41:59.700
Oh.
噢。

1043
00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:02.140
Okay, let me take another sip.
好吧，让我再喝一口。

1044
00:42:02.680 --> 00:42:04.220
All areas of the tongue.
舌头的各个部位都感受到了。

1045
00:42:06.180 --> 00:42:07.040
Between the two.
两者之间。

1046
00:42:07.180 --> 00:42:10.800
It makes my mouth want to expel it.
这味道让我嘴里想把它吐出来。

1047
00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:12.320
I want to-
我想——

1048
00:42:12.320 --> 00:42:18.500
I don't know if it's because I've had the mayonnaise and olives, but I'm like, this ain't so bad.
我不知道是不是因为我之前吃了蛋黄酱和橄榄，但我感觉，这其实没那么糟。

1049
00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:19.220
Yeah, this is fine.
是啊，这还行。

1050
00:42:19.360 --> 00:42:21.280
Like, nothing can ever be as bad as that.
反正没什么能比那个更糟糕了。

1051
00:42:21.360 --> 00:42:23.640
Ainsley, Cassie, how did you like the punch?
安斯利，凯西，你们觉得这果汁怎么样？

1052
00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:31.660
It tastes exactly the way it looks, and kind of like what I imagine unicorn droppings to taste like.
尝起来跟看起来一模一样，感觉就像我幻想中独角兽粪便的味道。

1053
00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:32.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1054
00:42:32.960 --> 00:42:39.540
Yeah, it's way too tart, but it's close, but not as good as this punch my grandma makes for the holidays,
是啊，太酸了，虽然接近了，但没法跟我奶奶节日做的果汁比，

1055
00:42:39.540 --> 00:42:44.360
which is just high C, ginger ale, and sherbet.
她那个就是用高C果汁、姜汁汽水和果子露做的。

1056
00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:45.040
Oh.
噢。

1057
00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:48.520
And that's really sweet and yummy and highly recommend.
那个特别甜，特别好喝，强烈推荐。

1058
00:42:48.740 --> 00:42:49.020
Okay.
好吧。

1059
00:42:49.220 --> 00:42:49.760
But so much sugar.
但糖分太多了。

1060
00:42:49.940 --> 00:42:52.020
Well, Ainsley, you saw me make it.
好吧，安斯利，你看着我做的。

1061
00:42:52.160 --> 00:42:54.180
I measured it per the instructions.
我是按说明书上的量放的。

1062
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:55.500
You did.
确实是。

1063
00:42:55.500 --> 00:43:01.900
It looks like something like when our kids were young and we played potion, you know, like, make your own potion.
这看起来就像我们孩子小时候玩的那种药水游戏，你知道的，就是自己调配药水。

1064
00:43:02.100 --> 00:43:05.760
And it was like, what do we got in the kitchen that I'll let them pour into a cup?
当时就是想，厨房里有什么东西是我能让他们倒进杯子里的？

1065
00:43:05.860 --> 00:43:09.540
Oh, you know what it looks like when you get one of those lush bath bombs?
噢，你知道它看起来像什么吗？就像那种奢华的沐浴炸弹？

1066
00:43:09.780 --> 00:43:10.040
Yes.
没错。

1067
00:43:10.200 --> 00:43:10.600
Yes.
是的。

1068
00:43:10.820 --> 00:43:13.240
And it gets all frothy and rainbowy and then-
弄得满是泡沫，五颜六色的，然后——

1069
00:43:13.240 --> 00:43:14.080
And like stains your bathtub.
还会把浴缸染上色。

1070
00:43:14.320 --> 00:43:14.580
Exactly.
就是这样。

1071
00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:21.060
Well, I guess Wookiees really like a tart drink at the holidays, but-
好吧，我想伍基人可能真的很喜欢节日里喝这种酸味饮料，但是——

1072
00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:21.120
Woo!
呜！

1073
00:43:21.300 --> 00:43:23.280
Okay, so I recommend the Bantha Surprise.
好了，我推荐“班萨惊喜”。

1074
00:43:23.280 --> 00:43:26.860
I would pass on the Joe Blasto punch.
至于“乔·布拉斯特”果汁，我还是算了吧。

1075
00:43:27.160 --> 00:43:29.060
I'm not hating the punch.
我倒不是讨厌这果汁。

1076
00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:29.860
Okay.
好吧。

1077
00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:31.600
All right, everybody.
好了，各位。

1078
00:43:31.980 --> 00:43:33.780
Well, let's keep going with our breakdown.
我们继续往下拆解吧。

1079
00:43:33.780 --> 00:43:37.880
But I want to say I haven't hated this experience.
但我得说，我并不讨厌这次体验。

1080
00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:46.840
I feel like maybe my tone so far is communicating a type of grumpiness.
我觉得我刚才的语气可能传达出了一种暴躁的感觉。

1081
00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:49.320
That's the highest compliment Jenna Fisher can give.
那可是珍娜·费舍尔能给出的最高评价了。

1082
00:43:50.200 --> 00:43:51.740
I didn't hate it.
我不讨厌它。

1083
00:43:51.740 --> 00:43:54.200
I, you know, it's-
我，你知道，它——

1084
00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:58.760
This experience, I look back on it with fondness in a way.
这次体验，回想起来我甚至觉得还有点美好。

1085
00:43:59.180 --> 00:43:59.760
Anyway.
总之。

1086
00:44:00.080 --> 00:44:00.420
All right.
好吧。

1087
00:44:01.300 --> 00:44:10.200
We're going to get back on the Millennium Falcon again and Han Solo is still having a hard time getting Chewie to his home planet.
我们要再次回到千年隼号上了，汉·索罗还在为送楚巴卡回母星而发愁。

1088
00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:15.700
Well, lady, the coordinates weren't the best and they came out of hyperspace into an Imperial convoy.
好吧，女士，坐标不太准，他们从超空间跳出来时正好撞进了一个帝国护航队。

1089
00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:18.460
I've got some gems from Han Solo.
我从汉·索罗那里搜集了一些金句。

1090
00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:20.060
How about this line?
这句怎么样？

1091
00:44:20.260 --> 00:44:23.320
This is one life day we won't soon forget.
这是我们难忘的一个生命日。

1092
00:44:23.620 --> 00:44:23.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1093
00:44:24.300 --> 00:44:29.920
And this one, why do I always think taking you home for life day is going to be easy?
还有这句，为什么我总觉得带你回家过生命日会很容易？

1094
00:44:30.780 --> 00:44:32.260
Why does he always think that?
为什么他总是这么想？

1095
00:44:32.360 --> 00:44:32.980
I don't know.
我不知道。

1096
00:44:33.140 --> 00:44:33.780
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1097
00:44:34.160 --> 00:44:36.520
I just lost control of the remote cannons.
我刚失去了对遥控炮塔的控制。

1098
00:44:36.540 --> 00:44:38.880
I got to go to the back and operate them manually.
我得去后面手动操作它们。

1099
00:44:39.880 --> 00:44:41.620
How do you operate them manually?
你怎么手动操作它们？

1100
00:44:42.020 --> 00:44:42.520
I don't know.
我不知道。

1101
00:44:42.660 --> 00:44:43.460
We're never going to see.
我们永远也见不到了。

1102
00:44:43.640 --> 00:44:43.780
No.
不。

1103
00:44:43.780 --> 00:44:44.960
We don't spend too much time.
我们花的时间不够多。

1104
00:44:45.280 --> 00:44:48.740
Well, now the Empire is going to declare martial law.
好吧，现在帝国要宣布戒严了。

1105
00:44:49.200 --> 00:44:53.240
No ships are going to be permitted in or out without further notice.
在另行通知前，任何飞船都不准进出。

1106
00:44:53.240 --> 00:44:54.500
I have one thing to say.
我有一件事要说。

1107
00:44:54.860 --> 00:44:55.280
One thing?
一件事？

1108
00:44:55.440 --> 00:44:55.740
Go ahead.
说吧。

1109
00:44:56.660 --> 00:45:01.520
The number of times the Empire has to pop on your TV screen, it's constant.
帝国出现在你电视屏幕上的次数，简直没完没了。

1110
00:45:01.540 --> 00:45:03.760
They're popping up all the time to tell you something.
他们总是突然冒出来告诉你些什么。

1111
00:45:04.040 --> 00:45:05.580
I'm like, can you turn it off?
我就想，能不能把它关掉？

1112
00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:06.500
I know.
我知道。

1113
00:45:06.500 --> 00:45:10.220
Do you have to have these people just popping up at your bar, at your home?
难道这些人非得在你的酒吧、你的家里这样突然冒出来吗？

1114
00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:12.420
Also, I guess they can see you.
而且，我猜他们能看见你。

1115
00:45:12.580 --> 00:45:14.540
They can just pop up and they see you.
他们随时都能冒出来，而且能看见你。

1116
00:45:14.700 --> 00:45:20.260
Like, what if you're walking through your house like post-shower and they just pop up on your screen?
比如，如果你刚洗完澡在家里走动，他们突然出现在屏幕上怎么办？

1117
00:45:20.260 --> 00:45:21.760
I didn't think they could see you.
我以为他们看不见你。

1118
00:45:21.760 --> 00:45:23.400
I thought you could only see them.
我以为只能你看见他们。

1119
00:45:24.180 --> 00:45:25.380
Well, it's not clear.
嗯，这还不清楚。

1120
00:45:25.540 --> 00:45:26.480
It's not clear.
还不清楚。

1121
00:45:27.900 --> 00:45:32.820
Well, now Sean Dan is going to come over to the Wookiee home.
好吧，现在肖恩·丹要来伍基人的家里了。

1122
00:45:33.060 --> 00:45:33.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1123
00:45:33.440 --> 00:45:39.980
He's got a toy for Lumpy and I thought it was a sewing machine for Mala, but it's not.
他给兰比带了个玩具，我本以为那是给玛拉的缝纫机，但并不是。

1124
00:45:39.980 --> 00:45:41.160
It's a projector.
那是个投影仪。

1125
00:45:41.680 --> 00:45:45.400
I don't know what he gives Mala, but before he gives her the gift.
我不知道他给了玛拉什么，但在他送礼物之前。

1126
00:45:45.560 --> 00:45:49.240
She got to give him a little kiss on the cheek.
她得在他的脸颊上亲一下。

1127
00:45:49.720 --> 00:45:51.820
For a gift she didn't ask for.
就为了一个她根本没要的礼物。

1128
00:45:52.320 --> 00:45:58.660
Why, why, why doesn't Sean Dan's shirt have a button or a zipper?
为什么，为什么，为什么肖恩·丹的衬衫没有扣子或拉链？

1129
00:45:58.940 --> 00:46:00.880
It is like all the way to his navel.
它一直开到他的肚脐眼。

1130
00:46:01.040 --> 00:46:01.600
It is open.
它是敞开的。

1131
00:46:01.800 --> 00:46:02.540
It's very open.
敞开得太夸张了。

1132
00:46:02.820 --> 00:46:04.140
A lot of open real estate there.
那儿露出的面积可真够大的。

1133
00:46:04.300 --> 00:46:04.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1134
00:46:04.480 --> 00:46:14.720
He is going to give Itchy a proton pack so that he can get his mind evaporator working.
他要给伊奇一个质子背包，好让他的思维蒸发器运转起来。

1135
00:46:15.100 --> 00:46:15.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1136
00:46:15.460 --> 00:46:19.740
It's like he sits down in like an old timey hair salon dryer.
他就像坐在那种老式的理发店烘发机下面一样。

1137
00:46:20.260 --> 00:46:26.340
And, you know, he kind of leans down to Itchy and kind of smirks and goes, I mean, this is wow.
然后，你知道，他凑近伊奇，带着那种坏笑说，我是说，这真是哇哦。

1138
00:46:26.640 --> 00:46:29.400
And then if you know what I mean, happy life day.
如果你懂我的意思的话，生命日快乐。

1139
00:46:29.560 --> 00:46:31.380
And I do mean happy life day.
我是说真的，生命日快乐。

1140
00:46:31.520 --> 00:46:33.620
I'm like, what's with the creepy dialogue?
我就想，这毛骨悚然的对话是怎么回事？

1141
00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:35.880
And what's with the creepy dialogue?
这毛骨悚然的对话到底是怎么回事？

1142
00:46:36.300 --> 00:46:39.640
It's foreshadowing for what we're about to see.
这是在为我们即将看到的内容做铺垫。

1143
00:46:39.860 --> 00:46:41.040
Here's what happens.
接下来发生的事是这样的。

1144
00:46:41.600 --> 00:46:44.700
Itchy puts this virtual reality headset on.
伊奇戴上了这个虚拟现实头盔。

1145
00:46:44.920 --> 00:46:46.400
He sits under it.
他坐在下面。

1146
00:46:46.520 --> 00:46:47.620
It's like a hairdryer.
就像个烘发机。

1147
00:46:47.620 --> 00:46:47.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1148
00:46:48.340 --> 00:46:57.460
And then Mermia is this very sexy holographic image played by Diane Carroll.
然后默米亚出现了，那是一个由黛安·卡罗尔扮演的非常性感的全息影像。

1149
00:46:57.760 --> 00:46:59.300
I just want you guys to hear.
我只是想让你们听听。

1150
00:46:59.500 --> 00:47:01.660
I want you to hear some of the things she's saying.
我想让你们听听她说的一些话。

1151
00:47:01.960 --> 00:47:02.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1152
00:47:02.140 --> 00:47:03.320
Let's just listen to it.
我们来听听看吧。

1153
00:47:03.920 --> 00:47:07.360
She's wearing a sparkly wig and this off the shoulder gown.
她戴着一顶闪亮的假发，穿着这件露肩礼服。

1154
00:47:07.580 --> 00:47:10.440
So just imagine Diane Carroll looking incredible.
所以，想象一下戴安·卡罗尔看起来有多迷人。

1155
00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:11.140
Very, very sexy.
非常、非常性感。

1156
00:47:11.320 --> 00:47:12.180
And Bob Mackie.
还有鲍勃·麦基的设计。

1157
00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:16.540
This is the gift that Sean gives to the grandpa.
这是肖恩送给爷爷的礼物。

1158
00:47:16.900 --> 00:47:17.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1159
00:47:17.520 --> 00:47:17.600
Yeah.
没错。

1160
00:47:17.620 --> 00:47:19.420
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

1161
00:47:20.180 --> 00:47:22.640
I can feel my creation.
我能感受到我的创作。

1162
00:47:24.540 --> 00:47:26.380
I'm getting your message.
我收到你的讯息了。

1163
00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:28.040
Are you getting mine?
你收到我的了吗？

1164
00:47:29.980 --> 00:47:31.740
Oh, oh.
噢，噢。

1165
00:47:32.100 --> 00:47:34.700
We are excited, aren't we?
我们很兴奋，对吧？

1166
00:47:35.640 --> 00:47:36.920
Well, just relax.
好了，放松点。

1167
00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:38.120
Just relax.
放松点。

1168
00:47:38.640 --> 00:47:38.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1169
00:47:40.980 --> 00:47:45.720
We can have a good time.
我们可以玩得很开心。

1170
00:47:51.350 --> 00:47:52.430
I'll tell you a secret.
我告诉你一个秘密。

1171
00:47:52.430 --> 00:48:10.790
She's rewinding it.
她在倒带。

1172
00:48:10.910 --> 00:48:12.330
She says it over and over.
她一遍又一遍地说着。

1173
00:48:12.730 --> 00:48:14.670
This is crazy to me.
这对我来说太疯狂了。

1174
00:48:14.870 --> 00:48:18.210
Grandpa is sitting in the middle of the kitchen getting off.
爷爷坐在厨房中间，正乐在其中。

1175
00:48:18.510 --> 00:48:19.590
Happy holidays.
节日快乐。

1176
00:48:20.330 --> 00:48:23.910
She's going to go on to say things like, I am your fantasy.
她接下来会说诸如“我是你的幻想”之类的话。

1177
00:48:24.330 --> 00:48:26.210
I am your experience.
“我是你的体验。”

1178
00:48:26.710 --> 00:48:28.170
I am your pleasure.
“我是你的快乐。”

1179
00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:30.050
Experience me.
“来体验我吧。”

1180
00:48:31.390 --> 00:48:33.610
Then she's going to perform a song.
然后她要表演一首歌。

1181
00:48:33.610 --> 00:48:38.610
This was an original song written for the special called This Minute Now.
这是一首为特别节目《此时此刻》创作的原创歌曲。

1182
00:48:39.010 --> 00:48:42.370
And it is the least melodic song I've ever heard in my life.
而且这是我这辈子听过最没旋律感的歌。

1183
00:48:42.370 --> 00:48:44.210
And I thought we should listen to some of it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

1184
00:48:44.510 --> 00:48:44.690
Really?
真的吗？

1185
00:48:44.830 --> 00:48:47.750
Because there's one more coming up that's going to give it a run for its money.
因为后面还有一首，足以和这首一较高下。

1186
00:48:47.750 --> 00:49:05.940
If we could only bend this minute, infinitely extend this minute, then I could live my whole life.
如果我们能弯曲这一分钟，无限延长这一分钟，那我就可以过完我的一生。

1187
00:49:20.220 --> 00:49:22.180
Okay, I can't anymore with it.
好了，我受不了了。

1188
00:49:22.360 --> 00:49:23.300
Okay, that was enough.
好了，够了。

1189
00:49:23.520 --> 00:49:27.340
It sounds like when you sing to your cat or when you sing to your pets.
听起来就像你对着猫或者宠物唱歌一样。

1190
00:49:28.480 --> 00:49:29.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1191
00:49:29.400 --> 00:49:30.320
It does.
确实。

1192
00:49:30.500 --> 00:49:31.580
It really does.
真的太像了。

1193
00:49:33.600 --> 00:49:38.770
Can I talk to you, though, about Diane Carroll?
不过，我能跟你聊聊戴安·卡罗尔吗？

1194
00:49:39.630 --> 00:49:40.790
Yes, please.
请讲。

1195
00:49:41.630 --> 00:49:44.970
Diane Carroll is such a freaking badass.
戴安·卡罗尔真是个超级狠角色。

1196
00:49:45.430 --> 00:49:45.790
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1197
00:49:46.370 --> 00:49:51.390
She was an actress, a singer, a model, and an activiSt.
她是一位演员、歌手、模特和活动家。

1198
00:49:52.070 --> 00:49:54.970
She starred in this television show called Julia.
她主演了一部叫《朱莉娅》的电视剧。

1199
00:49:54.970 --> 00:50:04.690
Julia, and this role was significant because it was the first American television show to star a Black woman in a non-stereotypical role.
《朱莉娅》，这个角色意义重大，因为它是第一部由黑人女性担任主角且角色不带刻板印象的美国电视剧。

1200
00:50:05.310 --> 00:50:08.090
And she won the Golden Globe for her performance.
她还凭借这个角色赢得了金球奖。

1201
00:50:08.470 --> 00:50:10.910
She also received an Emmy nomination.
她还获得了艾美奖提名。

1202
00:50:11.270 --> 00:50:17.010
She didn't win, but she was the first Black woman nominated for a primetime Emmy Award.
她虽然没获奖，但她是第一位获得黄金时段艾美奖提名的黑人女性。

1203
00:50:17.010 --> 00:50:25.070
She was also the first Black woman to win the Tony Award for Best Actress in a Musical for her role in the musical No Strings.
她还是第一位凭借音乐剧《无弦》中的角色获得托尼奖最佳音乐剧女主角的黑人女性。

1204
00:50:25.450 --> 00:50:29.370
She's very famous for playing Dominique Devereaux in the primetime soap opera Dynasty.
她因在黄金时段肥皂剧《豪门恩怨》中饰演多米尼克·德弗罗而闻名。

1205
00:50:30.270 --> 00:50:32.730
And she has appeared on Grey's Anatomy.
她还出演过《实习医生格蕾》。

1206
00:50:33.150 --> 00:50:34.090
She's a badass.
她真是个狠角色。

1207
00:50:34.610 --> 00:50:37.070
She is an absolute powerhouse.
她绝对是个实力派。

1208
00:50:37.070 --> 00:50:42.290
And, you know, I'm sort of noting all of the cameo stars.
而且，你知道，我正在记录所有的客串明星。

1209
00:50:42.590 --> 00:50:44.490
The level of their fame.
他们的名气程度。

1210
00:50:44.990 --> 00:50:49.770
These were, like, huge gets for this Star Wars special.
对于这部《星球大战》特辑来说，这些人简直是大牌中的大牌。

1211
00:50:50.010 --> 00:50:50.230
Yeah.
没错。

1212
00:50:50.610 --> 00:50:52.590
And we haven't even gotten to Bea Arthur yet.
而且我们还没提到碧·亚瑟呢。

1213
00:50:52.770 --> 00:50:53.170
No.
没呢。

1214
00:50:53.690 --> 00:50:58.050
Well, now Princess Leia and C-3PO are going to contact the Wookiees.
好吧，现在莱娅公主和C-3PO要联系伍基人了。

1215
00:50:58.350 --> 00:51:04.010
And, lady, this conversation, it's like, I know we keep saying this where you're just kind of like, what?
天哪，这段对话，就像是，我知道我们一直在说，但你听了只会觉得，什么鬼？

1216
00:51:04.210 --> 00:51:05.490
I have to read it to you.
我得读给你听。

1217
00:51:05.590 --> 00:51:05.850
Okay.
好的。

1218
00:51:05.950 --> 00:51:06.890
I transcribed it.
我把它转录下来了。

1219
00:51:07.070 --> 00:51:07.270
Oh.
噢。

1220
00:51:07.530 --> 00:51:12.690
They come on the screen, and Princess Leia says to Mala, happy life day.
她们出现在屏幕上，莱娅公主对马拉说，生命日快乐。

1221
00:51:13.150 --> 00:51:17.930
And then Mala says a bunch of stuff, right?
然后马拉说了一堆话，对吧？

1222
00:51:18.170 --> 00:51:26.450
And then C-3PO translates and says, she says it might seem like a happy life day for you, but personally, she's seen happier ones.
接着C-3PO翻译说，她说对你来说这可能是个快乐的生命日，但就她个人而言，她见过更快乐的。

1223
00:51:27.250 --> 00:51:29.570
Princess Leia doesn't react at all.
莱娅公主完全没有反应。

1224
00:51:29.690 --> 00:51:31.930
She goes, I don't want to tie up the channels.
她说，我不想占用频道。

1225
00:51:32.070 --> 00:51:33.830
Can you put Wookiee or Han on the phone?
你能让伍基人或者汉接电话吗？

1226
00:51:34.350 --> 00:51:35.130
Like, what?
就像是，什么鬼？

1227
00:51:35.130 --> 00:51:35.910
What?
什么？

1228
00:51:36.090 --> 00:51:37.910
She's just told you she's upset.
她刚告诉你她很难过。

1229
00:51:37.910 --> 00:51:40.530
She's like, yeah, can you put someone else on the phone?
而莱娅却说，好吧，你能让别人接电话吗？

1230
00:51:40.930 --> 00:51:46.010
Then Mala says a bunch more stuff, and basically they find out that they haven't arrived yet.
然后马拉又说了一堆，基本上她们发现他们还没到。

1231
00:51:46.010 --> 00:51:47.350
There's been no communication.
没有任何通讯。

1232
00:51:47.350 --> 00:51:51.910
It's the same information that we started the special with.
这和我们特辑开头的信息一模一样。

1233
00:51:52.170 --> 00:51:52.390
Yes.
是的。

1234
00:51:52.590 --> 00:51:54.670
We have to repeat it over and over again.
我们不得不一遍又一遍地重复它。

1235
00:51:54.890 --> 00:51:55.170
Over and over again.
一遍又一遍。

1236
00:51:55.190 --> 00:51:58.030
Everyone who Mala calls or anyone who calls Mala.
马拉打给的每个人，或者打给马拉的每个人都是这样。

1237
00:51:58.030 --> 00:52:01.610
But guess what Princess Leia's reaction is to this?
但你猜莱娅公主对此有什么反应？

1238
00:52:01.770 --> 00:52:02.110
What?
什么？

1239
00:52:02.750 --> 00:52:04.850
She says, are you alone?
她说，你是一个人吗？

1240
00:52:05.190 --> 00:52:08.130
And Mala says, no, I have a friend here.
马拉说，不，我有个朋友在这里。

1241
00:52:08.190 --> 00:52:09.930
And Leia goes, can I talk to him?
然后莱娅说，我能和他说话吗？

1242
00:52:10.230 --> 00:52:10.750
Like, what?
就像是，什么鬼？

1243
00:52:10.910 --> 00:52:12.010
What the f***?
搞什么鬼？

1244
00:52:12.010 --> 00:52:13.030
Why?
为什么？

1245
00:52:13.230 --> 00:52:15.070
Why can't Mala speak for herself?
为什么马拉不能自己说话？

1246
00:52:15.670 --> 00:52:25.270
So now Sean Dan comes to the screen, and Leia asks him to take care of the Wookiees until Chewie's arrival, and that she'll be contacting him again soon.
所以现在肖丹出现在屏幕上，莱娅让他照顾好伍基人直到楚巴卡到达，并说她很快会再联系他。

1247
00:52:25.510 --> 00:52:27.090
She couldn't tell Mala that.
她就不能告诉马拉吗？

1248
00:52:27.290 --> 00:52:29.030
She couldn't say, hang tight.
她就不能说，坚持住吗？

1249
00:52:29.450 --> 00:52:29.970
Exactly.
没错。

1250
00:52:30.390 --> 00:52:31.870
Mala can understand her.
马拉明明能听懂她的话。

1251
00:52:32.050 --> 00:52:33.690
She could have just said that right to Mala.
她本可以直接跟马拉说的。

1252
00:52:33.810 --> 00:52:36.630
It's not like Sean Dan then translates it into Wookiee.
又不是说肖恩·丹还要把它翻译成伍基语。

1253
00:52:36.630 --> 00:52:37.190
Exactly.
没错。

1254
00:52:37.550 --> 00:52:41.730
It's just hilarious to me that Princess Leia just keeps saying, is there someone else I can talk to?
我觉得特别好笑的是，莱娅公主一直在问，我能和别人谈谈吗？

1255
00:52:42.990 --> 00:52:43.650
All right.
好了。

1256
00:52:43.710 --> 00:52:45.330
We're back on the Millennium Falcon.
我们回到了千年隼号上。

1257
00:52:45.670 --> 00:52:46.830
We're going to check in.
我们要去看看情况。

1258
00:52:47.630 --> 00:52:52.710
Han Solo decides they need to land on the north side of the planet for safety reasons.
汉·索罗决定为了安全起见，他们需要降落在星球的北侧。

1259
00:52:53.110 --> 00:52:55.370
There's just too much Imperial traffic.
那里的帝国军交通往来太频繁了。

1260
00:52:55.690 --> 00:52:57.070
It's going to be a long walk.
还要走很长一段路。

1261
00:52:57.190 --> 00:52:58.570
Chewbacca's not happy about it.
楚巴卡对此很不高兴。

1262
00:52:59.110 --> 00:53:03.650
Now there is a commotion in the Wookiee home.
现在伍基人的家里一阵骚动。

1263
00:53:03.650 --> 00:53:09.030
Mala and Lumpy assume that it is Chewbacca who has arrived at laSt.
马拉和兰皮以为是楚巴卡终于到了。

1264
00:53:09.370 --> 00:53:15.350
So she opens her front door only to discover two stormtroopers and an Imperial officer.
于是她打开前门，却发现外面站着两个冲锋队员和一个帝国军官。

1265
00:53:15.790 --> 00:53:16.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1266
00:53:16.290 --> 00:53:24.710
They sort of scan the place, and then they say, all right, this unit is occupied by four Wookiees, two males and one adult female and one male child.
他们大概搜查了一下，然后说，好吧，这间屋子住了四个伍基人，两个成年男性，一个成年女性，还有一个雄性幼崽。

1267
00:53:24.950 --> 00:53:26.390
Where is the other male?
另一个雄性在哪里？

1268
00:53:26.730 --> 00:53:27.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1269
00:53:27.510 --> 00:53:28.450
Where is he?
他在哪儿？

1270
00:53:28.650 --> 00:53:33.430
The first thing they're going to do is check out Sean Dan's identification, and it checks out.
他们做的第一件事就是检查肖恩·丹的身份证明，检查结果没问题。

1271
00:53:33.650 --> 00:53:34.870
But Lumpy is upset.
但兰皮很生气。

1272
00:53:34.970 --> 00:53:40.250
He kind of growls at the guard, and Sean is trying to get Mala to come in the kitchen because he has a plan.
他对着守卫低吼，肖恩试图让马拉进厨房，因为他有个计划。

1273
00:53:40.450 --> 00:53:51.070
He's going to try to distract the stormtroopers, and he plays that music video box, which I think is the gift that he gave her, for one of the stormtroopers,
他打算分散冲锋队员的注意力，于是他给其中一个冲锋队员播放了那个音乐视频盒，我想那是他送给她的礼物，

1274
00:53:51.090 --> 00:53:53.050
and he watches Jefferson Starship.
然后他看着杰斐逊星船乐队的表演。

1275
00:53:53.050 --> 00:53:57.530
I was very confused because what are they distracting them from?
我当时很困惑，因为他们为什么要分散他们的注意力呢？

1276
00:53:57.690 --> 00:54:03.450
They're keeping them in the home by engaging them in this music box.
他们通过这个音乐盒把他们留在了家里。

1277
00:54:03.590 --> 00:54:08.150
But really, everybody, this is an excuse to get a performance from Jefferson Starship.
但说真的，各位，这只是为了让杰斐逊星船乐队表演的一个借口。

1278
00:54:08.550 --> 00:54:12.330
Taking you back in time, Jefferson Starship was huge.
带大家回顾一下，杰斐逊星船乐队当年非常火。

1279
00:54:12.690 --> 00:54:18.830
They were originally Jefferson Airplane, and you might know their hit, Somebody to Love.
他们前身是杰斐逊飞机乐队，你们可能听过他们的热门歌曲《Somebody to Love》。

1280
00:54:18.830 --> 00:54:19.890
Let's take a listen.
让我们来听听看。

1281
00:54:20.490 --> 00:54:24.730
When the truth is found to be...
当真相被发现是……

1282
00:54:49.560 --> 00:54:50.380
That's right.
没错。

1283
00:54:50.700 --> 00:54:51.720
We love that.
我们喜欢那首歌。

1284
00:54:52.040 --> 00:54:52.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1285
00:54:52.520 --> 00:54:52.700
Right?
对吧？

1286
00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:54.120
They were a very popular band.
他们曾是一个非常受欢迎的乐队。

1287
00:54:54.260 --> 00:54:55.060
They're from San Francisco.
他们来自旧金山。

1288
00:54:55.320 --> 00:54:58.620
In fact, they were one of the pioneering bands of psychedelic rock.
事实上，他们是迷幻摇滚的先驱乐队之一。

1289
00:54:59.560 --> 00:55:08.280
Two songs from their breakout album, Surrealistic Pillow, were on Rolling Stone's list of 500 greatest songs of all time.
他们成名专辑《Surrealistic Pillow》中的两首歌登上了《滚石》杂志史上最伟大的500首歌曲榜单。

1290
00:55:08.840 --> 00:55:11.880
One was Somebody to Love, and the other was White Rabbit.
一首是《Somebody to Love》，另一首是《White Rabbit》。

1291
00:55:12.240 --> 00:55:13.340
Remember that song?
还记得那首歌吗？

1292
00:55:14.020 --> 00:55:24.400
But shortly before this special came out, they had broken up, and a few of the original band members created a new band called Jefferson Starship.
但在这次特别节目播出前不久，他们解散了，几位原乐队成员组建了一个新乐队，叫杰斐逊星船。

1293
00:55:25.380 --> 00:55:26.460
And they...
而他们……

1294
00:55:26.460 --> 00:55:27.320
Not an airplane.
不是飞机。

1295
00:55:27.720 --> 00:55:28.020
Nope.
没错。

1296
00:55:28.320 --> 00:55:29.400
Still a flying object.
依然是飞行物体。

1297
00:55:29.640 --> 00:55:29.880
Correct.
正确。

1298
00:55:30.320 --> 00:55:31.120
Still Jefferson.
依然是杰斐逊。

1299
00:55:31.460 --> 00:55:33.420
Not Jefferson submarine.
不是杰斐逊潜水艇。

1300
00:55:33.940 --> 00:55:34.600
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1301
00:55:34.860 --> 00:55:35.820
Flying in the air.
飞在空中。

1302
00:55:36.040 --> 00:55:36.640
Flying in the air.
飞在空中。

1303
00:55:36.840 --> 00:55:38.060
Could have been Jefferson Jet.
可能是杰斐逊喷气机。

1304
00:55:38.280 --> 00:55:39.260
Maybe.
也许吧。

1305
00:55:39.640 --> 00:55:39.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1306
00:55:40.380 --> 00:55:41.440
Jefferson Boeing.
杰斐逊波音。

1307
00:55:41.840 --> 00:55:43.320
Jefferson hot air balloon.
杰斐逊热气球。

1308
00:55:44.200 --> 00:55:45.220
Jefferson kite.
杰斐逊风筝。

1309
00:55:46.960 --> 00:55:48.800
All things that are in the sky.
所有在天上的东西。

1310
00:55:49.080 --> 00:55:50.860
They went with Jefferson Starship.
他们选了杰斐逊星船。

1311
00:55:51.460 --> 00:55:51.900
Jefferson Big Bird.
杰斐逊大鸟。

1312
00:55:52.380 --> 00:55:52.980
Stop.
停。

1313
00:55:53.720 --> 00:55:54.720
Jefferson Eagle.
杰斐逊老鹰。

1314
00:55:55.000 --> 00:55:56.240
This is making us loopy.
这让我们有点晕头转向了。

1315
00:55:56.420 --> 00:55:56.720
Okay.
好吧。

1316
00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:58.260
Breaking this down is making us loopy.
深究这些让我们晕头转向。

1317
00:55:58.380 --> 00:55:58.640
Okay.
好吧。

1318
00:55:59.260 --> 00:56:05.620
Well, in this special, they played a song that they wrote called Light the Sky on Fire.
在这个特别节目中，他们演唱了一首自己写的歌，叫《点燃天空》。

1319
00:56:06.200 --> 00:56:09.660
During production, though, the song was given a different title.
不过在制作过程中，这首歌曾用过另一个标题。

1320
00:56:09.840 --> 00:56:11.840
This was the working title of the song.
这是这首歌的暂定名。

1321
00:56:12.500 --> 00:56:14.780
So this is what would have been, like, on a script.
所以这大概就是剧本上会写的东西。

1322
00:56:15.080 --> 00:56:18.280
Like, now Jefferson Starship plays this song.
比如，现在杰斐逊星船要表演这首歌了。

1323
00:56:18.280 --> 00:56:27.920
They changed it to Light the Sky on Fire when they released it, but the working title was, and I can't believe this didn't stick.
他们发行时改成了《点燃天空》，但暂定名是——我真不敢相信这个名字没留下来。

1324
00:56:28.280 --> 00:56:32.080
Because it rolls off the tongue.
因为它朗朗上口。

1325
00:56:32.080 --> 00:56:33.720
It is.
确实。

1326
00:56:35.260 --> 00:56:36.300
It is.
确实。

1327
00:56:36.460 --> 00:56:38.240
It has parentheses in it.
它里面还有括号。

1328
00:56:38.440 --> 00:56:38.860
It is.
确实。

1329
00:56:39.980 --> 00:56:41.760
Cigar-shaped object.
雪茄状物体。

1330
00:56:42.680 --> 00:56:43.440
Parentheses.
括号。

1331
00:56:43.760 --> 00:56:45.100
Vanished without a trace.
消失得无影无踪。

1332
00:56:46.040 --> 00:56:46.800
What?
什么？

1333
00:56:47.160 --> 00:56:50.280
Can you believe that that name didn't stick?
你能相信那个名字没留下来吗？

1334
00:56:50.660 --> 00:56:52.260
Cigar-shaped object?
雪茄状物体？

1335
00:56:52.260 --> 00:56:58.020
Cigar-shaped object vanished without a trace, was the original title of the song.
《雪茄状物体消失得无影无踪》是这首歌最初的标题。

1336
00:56:58.580 --> 00:57:04.900
This appearance marked Marty Balin's final appearance with Jefferson Starship.
这次亮相是马蒂·巴林最后一次以杰斐逊星船成员身份出现。

1337
00:57:05.580 --> 00:57:08.580
He was one of the members who broke off.
他是脱离乐队的成员之一。

1338
00:57:08.580 --> 00:57:14.620
The lyrics of the song mention a, quote, great god.
歌词里提到了一个，引用一下，伟大的神。

1339
00:57:15.020 --> 00:57:16.840
I didn't get the cigar.
我没听懂雪茄那个梗。

1340
00:57:17.380 --> 00:57:19.340
Oh, here, this might be it.
哦，给你，可能就是这个。

1341
00:57:19.520 --> 00:57:26.220
They mention a great god named Copacan who, quote, came from the stars and vanished.
他们提到了一个叫科帕坎的伟大神灵，引用一下，来自群星并消失了。

1342
00:57:26.620 --> 00:57:30.080
So is Copacan cigar-shaped?
所以科帕坎是雪茄形状的吗？

1343
00:57:30.520 --> 00:57:32.200
Who is Copacan?
科帕坎是谁？

1344
00:57:32.200 --> 00:57:36.240
Do we hear about this person later in Star Wars?
我们之后在《星球大战》里还会听到这个人吗？

1345
00:57:36.520 --> 00:57:38.360
Not that comes from memory.
据我记忆所及，没有。

1346
00:57:38.580 --> 00:57:39.140
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1347
00:57:39.760 --> 00:57:40.320
Okay.
好吧。

1348
00:57:40.600 --> 00:57:47.320
Well, the version that they played on the special was never released, but a shortened single was released.
他们在特别节目中演唱的版本从未发行，但发行了一个缩短后的单曲版。

1349
00:57:47.880 --> 00:57:54.200
But rather than listen to it, Angela, I would like to instead take you back to the late 80s.
但安吉拉，比起听那首歌，我更想带你回到80年代末。

1350
00:57:55.080 --> 00:57:57.300
To your middle school mixer.
回到你的中学舞会。

1351
00:57:57.620 --> 00:57:58.060
Okay.
好吧。

1352
00:57:58.400 --> 00:58:02.880
So that we can listen to this song by Jefferson Starship.
这样我们就能听杰斐逊星船乐队的这首歌了。

1353
00:58:03.400 --> 00:58:04.740
We built this city.
我们建造了这座城市。

1354
00:58:07.530 --> 00:58:08.290
You're welcome.
不客气。

1355
00:58:08.710 --> 00:58:11.430
We built this city.
我们建造了这座城市。

1356
00:58:11.630 --> 00:58:11.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1357
00:58:18.480 --> 00:58:18.900
All right.
好的。

1358
00:58:19.040 --> 00:58:20.160
I'll get up and dance with you.
我会起身和你一起跳舞。

1359
00:58:35.670 --> 00:58:36.510
That's right.
没错。

1360
00:58:38.030 --> 00:58:40.870
Get my high tops with my scrunchie socks.
穿上我的高帮运动鞋和堆堆袜。

1361
00:58:41.330 --> 00:58:41.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1362
00:58:41.890 --> 00:58:42.950
Crimp my hair.
把头发烫成波浪卷。

1363
00:58:43.250 --> 00:58:44.830
We needed this palette cleanse.
我们需要这种调剂一下心情。

1364
00:58:44.830 --> 00:58:45.250
We did.
确实。

1365
00:58:45.410 --> 00:58:46.010
We really did.
真的太需要了。

1366
00:58:48.850 --> 00:58:50.270
We built this city.
我们建造了这座城市。

1367
00:58:50.550 --> 00:58:51.230
We did.
我们做到了。

1368
00:58:52.870 --> 00:58:59.110
That was the song that we couldn't wait to come on at the Mixers when I was in 7th and 8th grade.
那是我上七八年级参加舞会时，最盼望听到的歌。

1369
00:58:59.290 --> 00:58:59.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1370
00:59:00.750 --> 00:59:01.450
All right.
好的。

1371
00:59:02.310 --> 00:59:10.290
Well, we're basically going to go now from a five-minute musical performance to a 10-minute cartoon.
好吧，我们现在基本上要从五分钟的音乐表演转到十分钟的动画片了。

1372
00:59:10.530 --> 00:59:11.790
Well, here's what happened.
事情是这样的。

1373
00:59:12.030 --> 00:59:14.550
You know, Lumpy, he kind of growls at a guard.
你知道，兰比对着一名守卫咆哮。

1374
00:59:14.550 --> 00:59:17.270
And the stormtrooper's like, really mean.
那个冲锋队队员非常凶。

1375
00:59:17.430 --> 00:59:19.110
They shove Itchy to the ground.
他们把伊奇推倒在地。

1376
00:59:19.270 --> 00:59:20.530
Lumpy starts freaking out.
兰比开始惊慌失措。

1377
00:59:20.650 --> 00:59:22.990
The general says, keep them quiet or else.
将军说，让他们安静点，否则后果自负。

1378
00:59:23.490 --> 00:59:23.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1379
00:59:24.190 --> 00:59:24.950
Or else what?
否则会怎样？

1380
00:59:25.430 --> 00:59:28.590
So Mala puts on one of Lumpy's favorite cartoons.
于是马拉放了一部兰比最喜欢的动画片。

1381
00:59:28.810 --> 00:59:30.210
The stormtrooper walks over.
冲锋队队员走了过来。

1382
00:59:30.290 --> 00:59:31.490
He's like, what's this all about?
他问，这到底是怎么回事？

1383
00:59:31.750 --> 00:59:35.470
And then quickly, Lumpy pretends to be playing like a video game.
然后兰比赶紧假装在玩电子游戏。

1384
00:59:35.470 --> 00:59:39.590
And then when he walks away, it cuts to he's watching this cartoon.
等那人走开后，画面切到他正在看动画片。

1385
00:59:39.910 --> 00:59:44.670
Why he couldn't know that he's watching a cartoon, I don't know.
为什么那人会不知道他在看动画片，我也不清楚。

1386
00:59:44.810 --> 00:59:45.830
It's about the resistance.
那是关于抵抗军的。

1387
00:59:46.250 --> 00:59:46.950
That's probably why.
大概是因为这个吧。

1388
00:59:47.190 --> 00:59:48.050
Oh, so maybe it's like, right.
哦，所以也许是这样，没错。

1389
00:59:48.310 --> 00:59:54.370
But while he's watching the cartoon, the stormtroopers are going to supposedly search the residence.
但当他在看动画片时，冲锋队队员本应去搜查住所。

1390
00:59:54.670 --> 00:59:56.150
How big is the residence?
这住所到底有多大？

1391
00:59:56.150 --> 00:59:58.390
I can see the whole bottom floor.
我一眼就能看到整个底层。

1392
00:59:58.390 --> 01:00:00.690
And when they go upstairs, it looks like one bedroom.
他们上楼时，看起来只有一个卧室。

1393
01:00:00.870 --> 01:00:03.070
It's just Lumpy's room up there.
楼上只有兰比的房间。

1394
01:00:03.350 --> 01:00:03.670
It's not that large.
没那么大。

1395
01:00:04.250 --> 01:00:08.390
When the cartoon came on, it's called The Faithful Wookiee.
动画片开始时，片名叫《忠诚的伍基人》。

1396
01:00:08.410 --> 01:00:09.710
And I didn't watch it.
我没看。

1397
01:00:09.910 --> 01:00:11.270
I watched the whole thing.
我把它全看完了。

1398
01:00:11.430 --> 01:00:14.910
I just, I just, I couldn't watch it.
我只是，我只是，我实在看不下去。

1399
01:00:15.310 --> 01:00:16.050
I watched it.
我看了。

1400
01:00:16.150 --> 01:00:18.270
It's much better than the holiday special.
它比那个节日特辑好多了。

1401
01:00:18.610 --> 01:00:18.830
Truly.
确实。

1402
01:00:19.250 --> 01:00:21.630
If you're going to watch anything, just watch this.
如果你非要看点什么，看这个就行了。

1403
01:00:21.630 --> 01:00:29.310
Well, according to the Nielsen data, you can see that the ratings for the special fall off after the cartoon.
嗯，根据尼尔森的数据，你可以看到特别节目的收视率在动画片之后就下滑了。

1404
01:00:30.070 --> 01:00:32.930
People stayed for the cartoon and then they were like, I'm out.
人们看完动画片就走了，大概是觉得，我撤了。

1405
01:00:33.110 --> 01:00:36.810
You can find just the cartoon on YouTube now and you don't have to watch the special.
你现在可以在YouTube上只看那段动画，没必要看整个特别节目。

1406
01:00:37.130 --> 01:00:39.370
But basically, I'll sum it up for you.
不过基本上，我来为你总结一下。

1407
01:00:39.950 --> 01:00:44.370
Luke Skywalker, C-3PO, and R2-D2, they're searching for a talisman.
卢克·天行者、C-3PO和R2-D2正在寻找一件护身符。

1408
01:00:44.630 --> 01:00:50.290
And the Millennium Falcon crashes on the water moon of Pana with the main characters on board.
千年隼号坠毁在帕纳的水月上，主角们都在船上。

1409
01:00:50.290 --> 01:00:58.250
Then they run into Boba Fett, who saves Luke from a giant monster and he claims to be there to help them.
然后他们遇到了波巴·费特，他从巨型怪物手中救了卢克，并声称是来帮助他们的。

1410
01:00:58.370 --> 01:01:00.890
But as it turns out, he's actually working for Darth Vader.
但事实证明，他其实是为达斯·维达效力的。

1411
01:01:01.370 --> 01:01:02.750
Well, here's a fun fact.
嗯，这里有个有趣的事实。

1412
01:01:02.950 --> 01:01:07.030
This cartoon introduced the character of Boba Fett to the Star Wars universe.
这部动画片将波巴·费特这个角色引入了《星球大战》宇宙。

1413
01:01:07.390 --> 01:01:09.370
Well, some might think that.
嗯，有些人可能会这么想。

1414
01:01:10.730 --> 01:01:16.450
But yes, it introduced everyone to Boba Fett in a television medium, on a screen.
但没错，它确实是在电视媒介上，在屏幕上向所有人介绍了波巴·费特。

1415
01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:25.830
But some fans might be surprised to know that the very first proper public appearance of Boba Fett wasn't on the big screen or even on TV.
不过有些粉丝可能会惊讶地发现，波巴·费特第一次正式公开亮相并不是在大银幕上，甚至也不是在电视上。

1416
01:01:26.670 --> 01:01:32.230
Boba first appeared at a parade for the San Asilmo County Fair in September of 1978.
波巴第一次露面是在1978年9月的圣安塞尔莫县博览会的游行中。

1417
01:01:33.790 --> 01:01:35.050
He was in a parade.
他参加了一场游行。

1418
01:01:35.450 --> 01:01:39.050
Before he was ever on screen, he was in a parade.
在他出现在屏幕上之前，他先参加了游行。

1419
01:01:39.050 --> 01:01:41.270
How did anyone know who he was?
当时怎么会有人知道他是谁呢？

1420
01:01:42.210 --> 01:01:43.650
How did he end up in the parade?
他怎么会出现在游行队伍里的？

1421
01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:51.570
Well, I will tell you, there is a documentary called Under the Helmet, The Legacy of Boba Fett on Disney Plus, and it talks all about it.
嗯，我告诉你，Disney Plus上有一部纪录片叫《头盔之下：波巴·费特的遗产》，里面讲了这一切。

1422
01:01:51.830 --> 01:01:52.130
Huh.
哈。

1423
01:01:53.050 --> 01:01:54.510
Well, there you go.
你看，就是这样。

1424
01:01:55.530 --> 01:02:01.270
So, I have a question about the cartoon, because I did watch a little bit of it, and I am trying to wrap my head around it.
所以，我有个关于动画片的问题，因为我确实看了一点，我正试着理解它。

1425
01:02:01.410 --> 01:02:09.350
So, what's happening is, Lumpy is watching a cartoon about his actual dad.
所以，剧情是这样的，兰比正在看一部关于他亲生父亲的动画片。

1426
01:02:09.570 --> 01:02:13.150
Yeah, his dad must be famous, because his dad is Han Solo.
没错，他爸爸一定很有名，因为他爸爸是汉·索罗。

1427
01:02:13.150 --> 01:02:14.150
He's been made into a cartoon.
他被做成了动画角色。

1428
01:02:14.490 --> 01:02:14.790
Yeah, mm-hmm.
是的，嗯哼。

1429
01:02:15.210 --> 01:02:15.610
Okay.
好吧。

1430
01:02:15.830 --> 01:02:16.750
He loved it.
他很喜欢。

1431
01:02:16.910 --> 01:02:17.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1432
01:02:17.830 --> 01:02:25.670
Now, we're going to cut back and see that the Wookiee home is just being completely destroyed by the troopers and this officer.
现在，镜头切回来，我们看到伍基人的家被冲锋队和那个军官彻底毁了。

1433
01:02:26.210 --> 01:02:27.610
They found nothing.
他们什么也没找到。

1434
01:02:28.270 --> 01:02:32.910
They've trashed Lumpy's room, and then the officer is like, clean up your room.
他们把兰比的房间翻了个底朝天，然后那个军官居然说，把你的房间收拾干净。

1435
01:02:33.150 --> 01:02:33.870
Ha, ha, ha.
哈哈哈哈。

1436
01:02:34.030 --> 01:02:37.390
I think it's hilarious to trash a child's room.
我觉得把孩子的房间搞得一团糟真是太搞笑了。

1437
01:02:37.550 --> 01:02:38.410
So funny.
太好笑了。

1438
01:02:38.790 --> 01:02:44.070
They discover that Lumpy's stuffed animal, which was a bantha, had been decapitated.
他们发现兰比的毛绒玩具，那是个班萨兽，头被砍掉了。

1439
01:02:44.250 --> 01:02:45.330
Well, they ripped his head off.
嗯，他们把它的头扯了下来。

1440
01:02:45.330 --> 01:02:45.910
I know.
我知道。

1441
01:02:45.910 --> 01:02:47.390
Oh, they're jerks.
哦，他们真是混蛋。

1442
01:02:48.170 --> 01:02:51.870
Lumpy is now going to, for a reason I didn't understand.
兰比现在要去做一件事，原因我没看懂。

1443
01:02:52.050 --> 01:02:52.670
I don't get it.
我不明白。

1444
01:02:52.810 --> 01:02:59.290
He's going to watch an instructional video on how to rebuild his mini transmitter.
他要看一段教学视频，学习如何重建他的微型发射器。

1445
01:02:59.670 --> 01:03:04.830
You kind of just have to make the jump that the stormtroopers wrecked it, and now he's trying to fix it.
你只能默认是冲锋队把它弄坏了，现在他正试图修理它。

1446
01:03:04.870 --> 01:03:05.490
I guess.
我想是吧。

1447
01:03:05.790 --> 01:03:10.670
This is going to be another comedy bit from Harvey Korman.
这又是哈维·科曼的一段喜剧表演。

1448
01:03:11.630 --> 01:03:13.870
This is really just a bunch of physical comedy.
这其实就是一堆肢体喜剧。

1449
01:03:13.870 --> 01:03:18.930
It's the worst instructional video ever because the person giving it slowly –
这是史上最烂的教学视频，因为演示的人慢吞吞地——

1450
01:03:18.930 --> 01:03:20.050
He's a robot.
他是个机器人。

1451
01:03:20.070 --> 01:03:21.810
He's a robot who slowly shuts down.
他是个正在缓慢关机的机器人。

1452
01:03:21.810 --> 01:03:22.990
He's like malfunctioning.
他好像故障了。

1453
01:03:23.070 --> 01:03:24.610
Why would you publish this video?
你为什么要发布这段视频？

1454
01:03:24.890 --> 01:03:28.210
If you took this video, it's not live, right?
如果你拍了这段视频，那它不是直播，对吧？

1455
01:03:28.210 --> 01:03:30.690
It's not a live video, right?
这不是直播视频，对吧？

1456
01:03:30.690 --> 01:03:35.990
He's watching a video like if we went on YouTube to be like, how do I fix my dishwasher?
他看视频的样子，就像我们上YouTube搜“怎么修理洗碗机”一样。

1457
01:03:36.490 --> 01:03:38.710
And the one that you're watching is broken.
而你正在看的那个视频坏了。

1458
01:03:39.070 --> 01:03:41.070
It shorts out as you watch it.
你看着看着它就短路了。

1459
01:03:41.170 --> 01:03:43.850
Yes, the robot instructor keeps shorting out.
没错，那个机器人导师一直在短路。

1460
01:03:43.930 --> 01:03:45.070
Why would you post it?
你为什么要发出来？

1461
01:03:45.310 --> 01:03:50.170
Why wouldn't you get your robot in order before you posted the video?
为什么不在发布视频前先把你的机器人修好呢？

1462
01:03:51.110 --> 01:03:51.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1463
01:03:52.350 --> 01:03:52.590
Okay.
好吧。

1464
01:03:52.590 --> 01:03:56.970
But Harvey Korman does some really funny physical comedy here.
但哈维·科曼在这里的肢体喜剧表演真的很滑稽。

1465
01:03:57.210 --> 01:03:57.370
He does.
确实。

1466
01:03:57.570 --> 01:03:58.150
He does.
确实。

1467
01:03:58.630 --> 01:04:03.850
Now on the TV, I'm not sure why, but we're transmitted to Tatooine.
现在电视上，我也不确定为什么，我们被传送到了塔图因星球。

1468
01:04:04.230 --> 01:04:06.590
We're at Bea Arthur's bar.
我们在碧·亚瑟开的酒吧里。

1469
01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:07.710
Akmina.
阿克米娜。

1470
01:04:08.130 --> 01:04:10.230
Akmina is played by Bea Arthur.
阿克米娜由碧·亚瑟饰演。

1471
01:04:10.370 --> 01:04:11.690
She runs this bar.
她经营着这家酒吧。

1472
01:04:11.970 --> 01:04:14.250
She's tasked with managing the bar.
她的任务是管理这家酒吧。

1473
01:04:14.370 --> 01:04:15.150
It's very busy.
这里非常忙碌。

1474
01:04:15.150 --> 01:04:18.790
And now we have another character played by Harvey Korman.
现在又出现了一个由哈维·科曼饰演的角色。

1475
01:04:19.130 --> 01:04:21.350
His name is Krellman.
他的名字叫克雷尔曼。

1476
01:04:21.830 --> 01:04:27.330
He has six fingers and he drinks liquid by pouring liquid into the top of his head.
他有六根手指，喝东西时是把液体倒进头顶里。

1477
01:04:27.650 --> 01:04:31.890
He's going to come over and he's going to order a drink.
他走过来准备点一杯酒。

1478
01:04:32.030 --> 01:04:37.450
And I just really love Bea Arthur in this scene and I thought we should hear it.
我真的很喜欢碧·亚瑟在这一幕里的表现，我觉得我们应该听听这段。

1479
01:04:37.730 --> 01:04:40.510
She's not taking any of his BS.
她一点也不吃他那一套。

1480
01:04:41.910 --> 01:04:42.750
What'll I do?
我该怎么办？

1481
01:04:43.310 --> 01:04:44.610
Hello, Akmina.
你好，阿克米娜。

1482
01:04:45.350 --> 01:04:46.750
Okay, we'll do it your way.
好吧，按你的方式来。

1483
01:04:46.890 --> 01:04:47.030
Hello.
你好。

1484
01:04:47.430 --> 01:04:48.350
Now we'll do it my way.
现在按我的方式来。

1485
01:04:48.470 --> 01:04:48.970
What'll it be?
要点什么？

1486
01:04:49.390 --> 01:04:50.070
Can we talk?
我们能谈谈吗？

1487
01:04:50.890 --> 01:04:52.210
Well, of course we can talk.
当然可以谈。

1488
01:04:52.350 --> 01:04:53.230
We are talking.
我们正在谈。

1489
01:04:53.630 --> 01:04:54.670
You're not ordering.
你还没点单。

1490
01:04:54.870 --> 01:04:55.690
I'm not pouring.
我还没倒酒。

1491
01:04:55.950 --> 01:04:56.850
We are not drinking.
我们还没喝。

1492
01:04:57.150 --> 01:04:57.870
We are talking.
我们正在谈话。

1493
01:04:58.470 --> 01:05:03.150
I'm moving this to make room for a drink so that next time I say, what'll it be, and you
我把这个挪开是为了腾出地方放酒，这样下次我问“要点什么”时，你

1494
01:05:03.150 --> 01:05:04.650
tell me, I can put it right there.
告诉我，我就能直接放在那儿了。

1495
01:05:05.050 --> 01:05:05.530
It doesn't matter.
无所谓。

1496
01:05:05.770 --> 01:05:06.250
Give me anything.
随便给我来点什么。

1497
01:05:06.790 --> 01:05:07.550
I'll have one of those.
我要那个。

1498
01:05:09.010 --> 01:05:10.730
I'm sorry I couldn't get back before.
抱歉我之前没能回来。

1499
01:05:11.070 --> 01:05:11.730
Before what?
之前什么？

1500
01:05:12.550 --> 01:05:13.230
Until now.
直到现在。

1501
01:05:13.730 --> 01:05:16.810
Until tonight, I thought about it a dozen times, but I had to be sure.
直到今晚，我考虑过十几次，但我必须确定。

1502
01:05:17.090 --> 01:05:17.710
Excuse me.
不好意思。

1503
01:05:17.790 --> 01:05:18.650
I have a customer waiting.
我有位顾客在等。

1504
01:05:18.750 --> 01:05:19.250
I'll be right back.
我马上回来。

1505
01:05:20.330 --> 01:05:21.430
Come back soon.
快点回来。

1506
01:05:21.850 --> 01:05:22.870
I'll be waiting.
我会等着你。

1507
01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:24.430
I just love her.
我真是太喜欢她了。

1508
01:05:24.490 --> 01:05:27.750
I feel like she's the Joe Bennett of the Star Wars special.
我觉得她就像《星球大战》特辑里的乔·贝内特。

1509
01:05:28.010 --> 01:05:28.670
She is.
她确实是。

1510
01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:31.710
She's like, fine, we'll do it your way.
她就像是说，好吧，我们就按你的方式来。

1511
01:05:31.910 --> 01:05:32.190
Hello.
你好。

1512
01:05:32.530 --> 01:05:33.690
Now we'll do it my way.
现在我们要按我的方式来。

1513
01:05:33.830 --> 01:05:34.630
What do you have?
你有什么？

1514
01:05:34.910 --> 01:05:35.350
Exactly.
没错。

1515
01:05:35.950 --> 01:05:40.890
Well, you know, I read that Bea Arthur's performance by all the critics at the time was singled
嗯，你知道，我读到过当时所有的评论家都将碧·亚瑟的表演

1516
01:05:40.890 --> 01:05:43.070
out as a highlight of this holiday special.
挑出来作为这部节日特辑的亮点。

1517
01:05:43.150 --> 01:05:44.450
It was the highlight for me.
对我来说，这就是亮点。

1518
01:05:44.930 --> 01:05:45.990
This whole section.
整个这一段都是。

1519
01:05:46.170 --> 01:05:47.690
And this was all directed.
而且这一切都是由……执导的。

1520
01:05:47.850 --> 01:05:51.630
Her whole section, she's about to sing, was directed by the first director.
她唱歌前的整段戏，是由第一位导演执导的。

1521
01:05:51.630 --> 01:05:56.650
And I guess there are some rumors that the shoot was 24 hours.
我猜有一些传言说拍摄持续了24小时。

1522
01:05:56.990 --> 01:05:57.770
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1523
01:05:57.830 --> 01:06:00.750
It was a crazy, crazy shoot day.
那真是疯狂、疯狂的一天拍摄。

1524
01:06:00.990 --> 01:06:05.770
I saw in an interview that Bea Arthur said she was cast as Akmina thanks to her friendship
我在一次采访中看到碧·亚瑟说，多亏了她与肯和米兹·韦尔奇的友谊，

1525
01:06:05.770 --> 01:06:08.890
with Ken and Mitzi Welch, two of the show's producers.
她才得以出演阿克米娜这个角色，他们是该节目的两位制片人。

1526
01:06:09.210 --> 01:06:13.210
They also wrote the song, Good Night But Not Goodbye, which is the song that she's going
他们还写了《晚安但不是永别》这首歌，也就是她马上要唱的那首歌。

1527
01:06:13.210 --> 01:06:14.230
to sing in a second.
马上就要唱了。

1528
01:06:14.850 --> 01:06:18.370
Bea Arthur's commitment to the reality of the scene is really incredible.
碧·亚瑟对场景真实感的投入真是令人难以置信。

1529
01:06:18.810 --> 01:06:20.110
She is so fantastic.
她真是太棒了。

1530
01:06:20.110 --> 01:06:24.590
These Imperial Guards are going to come on the screen and they're going to impose a curfew.
这些帝国卫兵会出现在屏幕上，并强行实施宵禁。

1531
01:06:25.470 --> 01:06:27.030
Everyone has to leave the bar.
每个人都必须离开酒吧。

1532
01:06:27.310 --> 01:06:28.770
Yeah, she said, guys, we're closing.
是啊，她说，伙计们，我们要打烊了。

1533
01:06:28.950 --> 01:06:29.750
They're closing me down.
他们要让我关门了。

1534
01:06:29.850 --> 01:06:30.570
You got to leave.
你们得离开。

1535
01:06:30.830 --> 01:06:35.670
But everyone saw the Imperial Guard come on the screen and impose this curfew.
但每个人都看到了帝国卫兵出现在屏幕上并实施了宵禁。

1536
01:06:35.810 --> 01:06:37.750
It's not like she took a phone call in the back.
这又不是她在后台接了个电话。

1537
01:06:37.890 --> 01:06:40.410
No, they pop up on a screen like they do.
不，他们就像往常一样出现在屏幕上。

1538
01:06:40.810 --> 01:06:42.050
But no one will leave.
但没人愿意离开。

1539
01:06:42.190 --> 01:06:42.750
They don't care.
他们根本不在乎。

1540
01:06:42.970 --> 01:06:43.070
Why?
为什么？

1541
01:06:43.210 --> 01:06:44.150
Why won't they leave?
为什么他们不离开？

1542
01:06:44.290 --> 01:06:44.710
I don't know.
我不知道。

1543
01:06:44.930 --> 01:06:47.170
Why is she the only person afraid of this curfew?
为什么她是唯一一个害怕宵禁的人？

1544
01:06:47.310 --> 01:06:49.410
She's like begging them, you guys, you got to go.
她就像是在求他们，伙计们，你们得走了。

1545
01:06:49.410 --> 01:06:54.690
She's like, I'll give you one more round of drinks and I'm going to sing you a song and
她就像是说，我再给你们上一轮酒，然后我给你们唱首歌，

1546
01:06:54.690 --> 01:06:55.790
then you got to go.
之后你们就得走。

1547
01:06:56.130 --> 01:06:56.730
You got to leave.
你们必须离开。

1548
01:06:57.210 --> 01:06:59.050
She should have put on the holiday special.
她本该播放那个节日特辑的。

1549
01:06:59.890 --> 01:07:00.790
You know what?
你知道吗？

1550
01:07:01.030 --> 01:07:02.350
She didn't have it yet.
她当时还没拿到那个特辑。

1551
01:07:02.350 --> 01:07:03.290
She didn't have it yet.
她当时还没拿到那个。

1552
01:07:03.470 --> 01:07:04.430
She didn't know.
她还不知道。

1553
01:07:04.990 --> 01:07:06.970
Let me tell you a little bit about Bea Arthur.
让我来给你们讲讲碧·亚瑟（Bea Arthur）的一些事。

1554
01:07:07.510 --> 01:07:09.870
She was an actress, a comedian and a singer.
她是一位演员、喜剧演员和歌手。

1555
01:07:09.870 --> 01:07:15.370
She began her career on stage where she won a Tony for playing Vera in Mame.
她的职业生涯始于舞台，曾凭借在《妈妈》（Mame）中饰演维拉（Vera）一角赢得了托尼奖。

1556
01:07:15.550 --> 01:07:20.310
So she was really a famous stage actress, musical theater star.
所以她确实是一位非常有名的舞台剧演员、音乐剧明星。

1557
01:07:20.790 --> 01:07:26.310
By the time she did this special, she was very well known for being in the comedy series
在拍摄这期特别节目时，她已经因出演喜剧系列剧而广为人知，

1558
01:07:26.310 --> 01:07:29.390
All in the Family and Maud, for which she won an Emmy Award.
比如《全家福》（All in the Family）和《莫德》（Maude），并凭借后者获得了艾美奖。

1559
01:07:29.730 --> 01:07:32.150
The holiday special was pre-Golden Girls, though.
不过，这期节日特别节目是在《黄金女郎》（Golden Girls）之前拍摄的。

1560
01:07:32.650 --> 01:07:34.450
Here's a fun fact about Bea Arthur.
关于碧·亚瑟，有个有趣的事实。

1561
01:07:34.450 --> 01:07:39.290
She has received the third most Emmy Award nominations with nine.
她以九次提名位列艾美奖提名次数第三多。

1562
01:07:39.930 --> 01:07:41.870
Do you know who's received the most?
你知道谁获得的提名最多吗？

1563
01:07:42.570 --> 01:07:43.470
Lucille Ball?
露西尔·鲍尔（Lucille Ball）？

1564
01:07:43.850 --> 01:07:44.310
No.
不是。

1565
01:07:45.290 --> 01:07:46.550
Julia Louis-Dreyfus.
朱莉娅·路易斯-德瑞弗斯（Julia Louis-Dreyfus）。

1566
01:07:46.650 --> 01:07:47.390
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1567
01:07:47.390 --> 01:07:49.250
Has been nominated 11 times.
她被提名了11次。

1568
01:07:49.510 --> 01:07:51.830
Mary Tyler Moore has been nominated 10.
玛丽·泰勒·摩尔（Mary Tyler Moore）被提名了10次。

1569
01:07:52.170 --> 01:07:54.050
And Bea Arthur has been nominated 9.
而碧·亚瑟被提名了9次。

1570
01:07:54.710 --> 01:07:58.090
Like real chops in the special, everyone.
这期节目里大家真的很有实力。

1571
01:07:58.290 --> 01:07:58.390
Yeah.
没错。

1572
01:07:58.690 --> 01:08:01.370
Like serious, amazing talent showed up for this thing.
真的，非常有才华的人都来参加这个节目了。

1573
01:08:01.370 --> 01:08:04.450
Well, she does eventually get everyone to leave.
嗯，她最终还是让所有人都离开了。

1574
01:08:05.070 --> 01:08:12.130
And one other fun fact about this scene is that some of the same aliens that we saw in
关于这个场景，还有一个有趣的事实，就是我们在《星球大战》的酒馆里看到的那些外星人，

1575
01:08:12.130 --> 01:08:17.350
the cantina in Star Wars are in the cantina again, including the band.
又出现在了酒馆里，包括那个乐队。

1576
01:08:17.670 --> 01:08:18.950
Yes, I clocked that.
是的，我注意到了。

1577
01:08:19.530 --> 01:08:19.730
Yeah.
没错。

1578
01:08:20.070 --> 01:08:21.070
Do you know the band's name?
你知道那个乐队的名字吗？

1579
01:08:22.670 --> 01:08:23.850
No, I don't.
不，我不知道。

1580
01:08:24.390 --> 01:08:24.650
Okay.
好吧。

1581
01:08:25.830 --> 01:08:28.910
Figrin de Anne and the Modal Nodes.
菲格林·丹（Figrin D'an）和莫达尔节点乐队（Modal Nodes）。

1582
01:08:29.350 --> 01:08:30.010
Again.
又来了。

1583
01:08:31.450 --> 01:08:37.390
It's very similar to your, to my, to Billy.
这和你、我、比利（Billy）的风格很像。

1584
01:08:37.670 --> 01:08:38.470
What is it?
是什么？

1585
01:08:38.710 --> 01:08:39.110
Belly Welly?
贝利·威利（Belly Welly）？

1586
01:08:39.110 --> 01:08:41.930
I thought it was Betsy Belly Welly or something.
我以为是贝茜·贝利·威利（Betsy Belly Welly）之类的。

1587
01:08:42.110 --> 01:08:44.670
I'm telling you, maybe you and George Lucas, same brain.
我跟你说，也许你和乔治·卢卡斯（George Lucas）心有灵犀。

1588
01:08:45.870 --> 01:08:46.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1589
01:08:46.890 --> 01:08:48.530
We're really good at naming things.
我们真的很擅长起名字。

1590
01:08:48.770 --> 01:08:48.830
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1591
01:08:49.130 --> 01:08:50.570
To sound like snowfluckers.
听起来像雪花怪（snowfluckers）。

1592
01:08:50.890 --> 01:08:51.490
I know.
我知道。

1593
01:08:51.590 --> 01:08:52.330
Flunky Lunkies.
笨拙的小家伙（Flunky Lunkies）。

1594
01:08:54.030 --> 01:08:54.530
All right.
好吧。

1595
01:08:54.650 --> 01:08:56.670
Back at the Wookiee House, we hear an announcement.
回到伍基人（Wookiee）的房子，我们听到了一则广播。

1596
01:08:57.050 --> 01:09:00.230
The Imperial Guards are being told to return to base.
帝国卫队被告知要返回基地。

1597
01:09:00.850 --> 01:09:01.690
Return to base.
返回基地。

1598
01:09:01.790 --> 01:09:02.410
But are they?
但他们真的要回去吗？

1599
01:09:02.770 --> 01:09:03.870
Are they being told that?
他们真的收到了这个通知吗？

1600
01:09:03.870 --> 01:09:07.230
Or is it a trick from Lumpy, who got his little device working?
还是说这是兰比（Lumpy）的诡计，他把他的小装置修好了？

1601
01:09:07.430 --> 01:09:07.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1602
01:09:07.830 --> 01:09:08.630
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1603
01:09:08.790 --> 01:09:12.110
Again, there's just so much keeping up with the Imperial soldiers.
再说一次，要跟上帝国士兵的动向实在太难了。

1604
01:09:12.330 --> 01:09:13.490
There's so many announcements.
公告实在是太多了。

1605
01:09:13.770 --> 01:09:14.350
I know.
我知道。

1606
01:09:14.350 --> 01:09:16.050
I would just have announcement fatigue.
我光是听公告都要听累了。

1607
01:09:16.670 --> 01:09:20.790
Well, the stormtrooper goes upstairs and catches Lumpy on his device.
好吧，冲锋队上楼抓住了正在玩设备的兰比。

1608
01:09:20.970 --> 01:09:24.450
He takes it and he smashes it and he chases him downstairs.
他抢过设备砸碎，然后追着兰比下了楼。

1609
01:09:24.450 --> 01:09:27.810
And all of a sudden, guess who walks in the door?
突然，你猜谁走了进来？

1610
01:09:28.430 --> 01:09:29.730
Han and Chewbacca.
韩和楚巴卡。

1611
01:09:29.910 --> 01:09:30.850
They made it.
他们成功赶到了。

1612
01:09:31.050 --> 01:09:33.070
But the Imperials are still present.
但帝国军还在场。

1613
01:09:33.510 --> 01:09:36.330
Chewbacca immediately runs to protect Lumpy.
楚巴卡立刻跑过去保护兰比。

1614
01:09:37.030 --> 01:09:44.990
Han confronts this whole situation and he kills the stormtrooper by tricking him into falling off the balcony.
韩面对这种局面，他诱骗冲锋队掉下阳台，从而杀死了他。

1615
01:09:45.290 --> 01:09:49.650
This is probably why maybe they established how high up they were.
这大概就是为什么他们要特意交代阳台有多高吧。

1616
01:09:49.810 --> 01:09:50.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1617
01:09:50.290 --> 01:09:52.690
It's a very, very short fight.
这打斗真的非常非常短。

1618
01:09:52.690 --> 01:09:59.830
So all of this has been leading up to possibly one of the shortest fights I've ever seen in a movie.
所以这一切铺垫，最后竟然只换来了我电影里见过最短的打斗之一。

1619
01:10:00.370 --> 01:10:05.850
It's like two punches and a fake and then the guy's off the railing.
就像两拳加一个假动作，那家伙就掉下栏杆了。

1620
01:10:05.990 --> 01:10:06.810
And it's over.
然后就结束了。

1621
01:10:07.110 --> 01:10:08.190
Sometimes that's all it takes.
有时候这就够了。

1622
01:10:08.390 --> 01:10:09.650
I guess that's all it takes.
我想确实这就够了。

1623
01:10:10.130 --> 01:10:13.050
The Wookiees embrace each other and then there's this.
伍基人互相拥抱，然后就出现了这一幕。

1624
01:10:13.670 --> 01:10:14.230
Ouch.
哎哟。

1625
01:10:14.830 --> 01:10:17.290
What is happening between Chewie and his wife?
楚巴卡和他妻子之间发生了什么？

1626
01:10:17.750 --> 01:10:18.890
What was that?
那是什么？

1627
01:10:19.170 --> 01:10:20.010
I don't know.
我不知道。

1628
01:10:20.010 --> 01:10:25.610
First of all, it's like they're, they come together like they're going to kiss.
首先，他们凑在一起，看起来像是要接吻。

1629
01:10:25.790 --> 01:10:25.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1630
01:10:26.130 --> 01:10:27.570
But they don't kiss.
但他们没亲。

1631
01:10:27.790 --> 01:10:30.430
They just sort of breathe in each other's faces.
他们只是对着彼此的脸呼吸。

1632
01:10:30.670 --> 01:10:30.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1633
01:10:31.210 --> 01:10:37.470
Is it, was I meant to feel that as, what is it?
这是，我本该感受到什么吗，这到底是什么？

1634
01:10:38.410 --> 01:10:39.570
Is it longing?
是渴望吗？

1635
01:10:40.010 --> 01:10:42.010
Is it, is she mad?
还是说，她在生气？

1636
01:10:42.010 --> 01:10:45.290
Is she like, I'm still kind of grumpy because you.
她是那种，因为你，我还在闹别扭吗？

1637
01:10:45.510 --> 01:10:46.410
No, it looked tender.
不，看起来很温柔。

1638
01:10:46.690 --> 01:10:47.590
It looked tender.
看起来很温柔。

1639
01:10:47.910 --> 01:10:48.610
I don't, exactly.
我不知道，确实。

1640
01:10:48.610 --> 01:10:56.050
Anyone back there, did you, what, what was your take on the Chewie Mala embrace?
后面有人吗，你们，你们对楚巴卡和马拉的拥抱怎么看？

1641
01:10:58.280 --> 01:10:59.380
We've lost them.
我们失去他们了。

1642
01:10:59.620 --> 01:11:00.140
Please hold.
请稍候。

1643
01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:01.420
They've left.
他们走了。

1644
01:11:03.760 --> 01:11:06.400
Yeah, they just kind of breathe in each other's mouths for a minute.
是啊，他们就那样对着彼此的嘴呼吸了一分钟。

1645
01:11:06.940 --> 01:11:07.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1646
01:11:07.340 --> 01:11:07.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1647
01:11:07.880 --> 01:11:10.420
They don't ever kiss or maybe that's.
他们从来不接吻，或者说这就是……

1648
01:11:10.420 --> 01:11:11.300
Do Wookiees not kiss?
伍基人不接吻吗？

1649
01:11:11.520 --> 01:11:13.060
Maybe that's their form of kissing.
也许这就是他们的接吻方式。

1650
01:11:13.720 --> 01:11:14.700
No, Wookiees kiss.
不，伍基人会接吻的。

1651
01:11:15.060 --> 01:11:17.760
Wookiees gotta kiss and like, I don't know.
伍基人得亲热一下，我也不知道。

1652
01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:22.180
Mala's been making that dinner, worried about him and that's all she gets.
玛拉一直在做那顿晚餐，担心着他，结果就换来这个。

1653
01:11:22.180 --> 01:11:26.340
I like how quickly you guys were like, no, they kiss, let me tell you.
我喜欢你们刚才那种反应速度，不假思索地说“不，他们亲了，让我告诉你”。

1654
01:11:26.520 --> 01:11:32.800
No, Cassie, my thing was that I thought Mala was like giving him like a cold shoulder a little
不，凯西，我的意思是，我觉得玛拉当时对他有点冷淡，

1655
01:11:32.800 --> 01:11:32.980
bit.
有一点。

1656
01:11:33.060 --> 01:11:37.320
Like he came in to kiss, but like he could tell she was still a little pissed.
就像他凑过去想亲吻，但能感觉到她还在生气。

1657
01:11:37.560 --> 01:11:37.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1658
01:11:38.160 --> 01:11:38.760
Or something.
或者类似的情况。

1659
01:11:39.040 --> 01:11:39.760
I like that.
我喜欢这个解读。

1660
01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:40.800
I don't know.
我不知道。

1661
01:11:41.180 --> 01:11:43.880
He's got a really, you know, winter back later tonight.
他今晚还得赶在入冬前回来，你知道的。

1662
01:11:44.160 --> 01:11:45.060
I guess he does.
我想他是吧。

1663
01:11:45.480 --> 01:11:47.300
I love that you're writing backstory for it.
我喜欢你为这事编背景故事。

1664
01:11:49.700 --> 01:11:55.040
You know, the one thing that really got me is just, you know, how Han is like, hey, you
你知道，真正让我触动的一点是，韩说“嘿，

1665
01:11:55.040 --> 01:11:58.260
know, you guys are like family to me, you know.
你们对我来说就像家人一样”，你知道吧。

1666
01:11:58.960 --> 01:12:06.300
And then I'm sure in the stage direction, it said Mala looks at Han with adoration or
我敢肯定剧本说明里写着“玛拉深情地看着韩”

1667
01:12:06.300 --> 01:12:07.080
something like that.
之类的指示。

1668
01:12:07.220 --> 01:12:12.700
But if you zoom in on Mala's face, the look is so crazy.
但如果你放大看玛拉的脸，那表情简直绝了。

1669
01:12:13.260 --> 01:12:16.860
She's like, like the look is so crazy.
她那表情，真的太疯狂了。

1670
01:12:17.300 --> 01:12:17.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1671
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:19.480
Anyway.
总之。

1672
01:12:19.660 --> 01:12:23.020
Well, they don't make a lot of different facial expressions.
好吧，他们确实做不出太多不同的面部表情。

1673
01:12:23.280 --> 01:12:23.780
There's not a lot.
没多少表情变化。

1674
01:12:24.340 --> 01:12:25.520
Well, Han is going to leave.
总之韩要走了。

1675
01:12:25.660 --> 01:12:26.160
He's off.
他要出发了。

1676
01:12:26.400 --> 01:12:27.300
He's like, bye.
他说，再见。

1677
01:12:27.500 --> 01:12:28.160
He's got to go.
他得走了。

1678
01:12:28.280 --> 01:12:28.760
Lay us.
莱亚斯。

1679
01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:29.900
Killed that guy.
干掉了那家伙。

1680
01:12:30.140 --> 01:12:31.320
Where is he going for life?
他到底要去哪儿？

1681
01:12:31.520 --> 01:12:31.880
I don't know.
我不知道。

1682
01:12:31.960 --> 01:12:32.380
We don't know.
我们都不知道。

1683
01:12:32.440 --> 01:12:33.320
We'll see him later.
我们回头再看他。

1684
01:12:33.580 --> 01:12:36.240
Harrison Ford just looked happy to exit stage right.
哈里森·福特看起来只是很高兴能从舞台右侧退场。

1685
01:12:36.800 --> 01:12:42.240
But no sooner is the family reunited than another Imperial officer appears on the screen.
但一家人刚团聚，屏幕上又出现了一名帝国军官。

1686
01:12:42.420 --> 01:12:43.560
So many announcements.
好多公告啊。

1687
01:12:43.960 --> 01:12:45.280
Now this is an alert.
现在是警报。

1688
01:12:45.440 --> 01:12:46.300
There's a missing stormtrooper.
有个冲锋队员失踪了。

1689
01:12:46.880 --> 01:12:50.040
They've already discovered that this stormtrooper is missing.
他们已经发现这个冲锋队员不见了。

1690
01:12:50.440 --> 01:12:53.360
And this is why I think that they can't see you.
这就是为什么我觉得他们看不见你。

1691
01:12:53.780 --> 01:12:56.300
Because then Sean Dan is like, I got this.
因为接着肖恩·丹说，这事我来搞定。

1692
01:12:56.460 --> 01:12:57.740
He puts in his identification.
他输入了自己的身份信息。

1693
01:12:57.740 --> 01:13:00.980
He's like, he robbed me and went off to the foreSt.
他说，他抢劫了我然后跑进森林里去了。

1694
01:13:01.220 --> 01:13:02.680
And they're like, thank you very much.
他们就说，非常感谢。

1695
01:13:02.780 --> 01:13:04.340
We'll go send out a search party.
我们会派搜查队去的。

1696
01:13:04.920 --> 01:13:05.800
Case closed.
结案。

1697
01:13:06.060 --> 01:13:06.220
Done.
搞定。

1698
01:13:06.660 --> 01:13:07.660
Is it though?
真的是这样吗？

1699
01:13:07.900 --> 01:13:12.940
Are they just leaving this stormtrooper's body at the bottom of this tree thing?
他们就打算把这个冲锋队员的尸体留在树底下吗？

1700
01:13:12.940 --> 01:13:14.620
Where does that go?
那地方通向哪儿？

1701
01:13:15.340 --> 01:13:17.000
Also, how do you get up there?
还有，你是怎么上去的？

1702
01:13:17.440 --> 01:13:18.580
Is there an elevator?
有电梯吗？

1703
01:13:18.880 --> 01:13:21.120
How did you get on the front porch of this thing?
你是怎么到这东西的前廊上去的？

1704
01:13:21.380 --> 01:13:21.860
Oh.
噢。

1705
01:13:22.020 --> 01:13:25.500
It's just, it's built around a tree really high up.
它就是建在一棵树上，位置很高。

1706
01:13:25.640 --> 01:13:27.000
Like, do you zip line in?
你是滑索进去的吗？

1707
01:13:27.180 --> 01:13:29.980
How do you get to the balcony to the front door?
你是怎么到前门的阳台上去的？

1708
01:13:30.160 --> 01:13:31.300
Lady, you didn't zoom in?
女士，你没放大看吗？

1709
01:13:31.820 --> 01:13:32.100
No.
没有。

1710
01:13:32.440 --> 01:13:33.160
Is there a bridge?
有桥吗？

1711
01:13:33.380 --> 01:13:34.380
There's an escalator.
有自动扶梯。

1712
01:13:37.720 --> 01:13:39.580
You're, you're messing with me.
你是在拿我开涮吧。

1713
01:13:40.140 --> 01:13:41.660
Could you imagine that?
你能想象吗？

1714
01:13:41.860 --> 01:13:44.260
It was like, little escalator.
就像那种小型的自动扶梯。

1715
01:13:44.400 --> 01:13:44.860
What though?
到底是什么情况？

1716
01:13:45.040 --> 01:13:48.100
Seriously, are they going to bury this?
说真的，他们打算把这事儿掩盖过去吗？

1717
01:13:48.300 --> 01:13:51.240
They're just like, oh, they're tricked them.
他们就像是，噢，他们把他们骗了。

1718
01:13:51.520 --> 01:13:52.040
Like, what?
什么意思？

1719
01:13:52.300 --> 01:13:55.740
There's a lot of things you've got to just make a mental jump for.
有很多事情你得靠脑补才能接受。

1720
01:13:56.020 --> 01:13:56.260
Okay.
好吧。

1721
01:13:56.260 --> 01:13:57.740
These are two of them.
这两点就是其中之一。

1722
01:13:57.940 --> 01:13:59.680
How do you get into the tree house?
你到底是怎么进到树屋里的？

1723
01:13:59.980 --> 01:14:00.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1724
01:14:00.720 --> 01:14:01.600
What happened to the body?
那具尸体怎么处理了？

1725
01:14:02.080 --> 01:14:02.380
Okay.
好吧。

1726
01:14:02.680 --> 01:14:09.500
Well, with the danger now passed, Chewbacca's family prepares to attend the Life Day Festival.
好了，随着危险解除，楚巴卡一家准备去参加生命日庆典了。

1727
01:14:09.800 --> 01:14:14.580
There's these gold glowing orbs and they're wearing red robes.
那里有一些金色的发光球体，他们穿着红色的长袍。

1728
01:14:14.660 --> 01:14:16.220
They kind of look like they're in a church choir.
看起来有点像教堂唱诗班。

1729
01:14:16.220 --> 01:14:21.700
